WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:23.296
Introduction. The religious and mythic elements of German National Socialism often made the Third Reich look like a cult in power. The pageantry of Nazi rallies and their quasi-liturgical nature matched the extraordinary fervor of the huge crowds. Most participants were caught up in an intense atmosphere of collective excitement and self-surrender.

00:00:23.296 --> 00:00:34.560
Hitler's undoubted charisma and the careful development and cultivation of the Führerkult since the earliest years of the movement were crucial factors in building Nazi religiosity.

00:00:34.560 --> 00:01:08.181
Huge congregations, banners, sacred flames, processions, a style of popular and radical preaching, prayers-and-responses, memorials, and funeral marches were all essential props for the cult of race and nation. They supported the mission of Aryan Germany and victory over her enemies. The messianic figure of Adolf Hitler, the savior of Germany, towered over the entire project. National Socialist ideology was deeply shaped by radical religious ideas.

00:01:08.181 --> 00:01:20.384
The belief in a Jewish world conspiracy, supposedly supported by the infamous The Protocols of the Elders of Zion, created an image of a demonic enemy.

00:01:20.384 --> 00:01:53.920
Nazi anti-Semitism grew from this apocalyptic demonology. It blamed Jews for all ills, including liberalism, communism, moral corruption, and the collapse of the traditional world. The idea of national regeneration also had an apocalyptic spirit. Only the destruction of Jews could ensure Germany's salvation in a racially pure millennium. Alfred Rosenberg, the main Nazi Party ideologue, was an early promoter of the Protocols.

00:01:53.920 --> 00:02:29.077
He established their central place in Nazi philosophy in the early 1920s. Dietrich Eckart, Hitler's mentor in Munich, held a gnostic-dualist view of Jews and their opposing role in German national life. Hitler's belief in a Jewish world conspiracy was a lifelong conviction. It found terrible fulfillment in the Holocaust. In an earlier book, The Occult Roots of Nazism, I traced ideas of racial election, demonology, and the millennium among Austrian German nationalists before the First World War.

00:02:29.077 --> 00:03:06.368
That study aimed to show how quasi-religious and even occult ideas could support German identity. They did so in response to perceived threats from liberalism, laissez-faire capitalism, and the rise of subject nationalities at the start of the last century. At that time, traditional groups saw large-scale industry, new metropolitan cities, the growth of capitalist finance, and organized labor as threats. These völkisch Ariosophists offered a defensive ideology of "Aryan" German folk identity.

00:03:06.368 --> 00:03:36.405
They presented it as a cure for unwelcome, disruptive challenges to traditional status, custom, and political authority. Against the rise of anthropology and eugenics, these sectarians embraced ideas of race. They stigmatized Jews as the supposed agents and beneficiaries of liberalism and modernity. Their occult notions of racial superiority combined with anti-Semitism and millenarian myths of national regeneration.

00:03:36.405 --> 00:03:46.133
This mix found its ultimate expression in the ideology of the National Socialist movement. Multicultural societies face a similar challenge today.

00:03:46.133 --> 00:04:22.059
In 1900, white Europeans made up about 35 percent of the world's population. White birth rates have fallen in advanced industrial nations. At the same time, populations in the Third World have exploded. Better medicine, sanitation, and industrialization drove this growth. Today, white Europeans make up just under 10 percent of the global population. Guest workers, immigrants, economic migrants, refugees, and asylum seekers form major population flows.

00:04:22.059 --> 00:04:30.933
These groups bring the population surplus of developing countries into lands traditionally settled by white people of European descent.

00:04:30.933 --> 00:05:03.957
Advanced industrial economies absorb ever larger levels of immigration. Their political commitment to multiracialism is now an article of faith. Today, the United States and most European nations face a demographic shift against their historic native stocks. The resulting issue of white identity repeats the dilemma of Austrian Germans. They feared a loss of influence in the old Habsburg Empire. Black Sun looks at how "Aryan" racial ideas have survived and returned.

00:05:03.957 --> 00:05:33.141
This happened in response to the challenges of the postwar world. More than fifty years after the defeat and disgrace of Nazism and fascism, the far right is again challenging the liberal order of Western democracies. It seeks political space. Radical ideologies feed on the threats of economic globalization, affirmative action, and Third World immigration. The book explores the far edges of right-wing extremist ideology.

00:05:33.141 --> 00:05:58.059
Aryan cults, aristocratic paganism, anti-Semitic demonology, Eastern religion, and the occult supply underground beliefs. These beliefs serve individuals and groups. These people fear a loss of status, cultural tradition, and identity. This fear arises in the emerging multicultural societies of the United States and Europe.

00:05:58.059 --> 00:06:05.056
The scene begins with a historical review of neo-Nazism in the United States and Britain.

00:06:05.056 --> 00:06:37.568
There, Nazism returned as an extreme reaction to communism, liberalism, and especially the desegregation of African Americans and other colored immigrants. In their search for a radical opposing ideology, American and British neo-Nazis supported Hitler and National Socialism against liberalism and the presence of ethnic minorities. Their underground publications praise National Socialism as a racial policy to ensure the global dominance of the white race forever.

00:06:37.568 --> 00:07:11.275
However, despite their main focus on colored races, neo-Nazi ideology still viewed Jews as the demonic enemy of white Aryan peoples. They see Jews as the architects of a multiracial world order. This order supposedly dissolves all nations, traditions, and loyalties before the final achievement of Jewish world conquest. The persistence of anti-Semitism in modern racist talk, which mainly targets ethnic groups, shows that the demonology of Nazism endures.

00:07:11.275 --> 00:07:44.299
Like Gnostics separated from a higher god in a dark world, American and British neo-Nazis claim that Hitler and Nazism are the only hope for the racial survival of white nations filled with growing ethnic minorities. Anti-Semitism acts as a Manichaean dualist heresy that splits the world into forces of good and evil. Millenarian racial cleansing and the belief in a Jewish world conspiracy are the defining moments of this neo-Nazi religiosity.

00:07:44.299 --> 00:07:51.808
From the 1950s to the 1970s, neo-fascist and neo-Nazi groups copied the past.

00:07:51.808 --> 00:08:24.405
They used uniformed members, swastika flags, and marches. Fringe political parties stayed the domain of fanatics. Recruitment was strictly limited to people who admired fascism or were convinced anti-Semites. Even when German nationalism became a global ideology of white racism, the history and politics of Nazi Germany remained the main model to copy. This loyalty to history marked the neo-Nazi cults linked to George Lincoln Rockwell and Colin Jordan.

00:08:24.405 --> 00:08:58.965
It also marked their successors and followers in the postwar Anglo-American world. Bound by the memory of German National Socialism, Anglo-American neo-Nazis stayed trapped in a nostalgic cult of Hitler worship. Universal condemnation of the Third Reich and the Holocaust blocked any chance of political success. Like the Ariosophists in the early 1900s, political isolation in a hostile, liberal world pushed many neo-Nazi and neo-fascist groups toward occult ideas of ancient Aryan wisdom.

00:08:58.965 --> 00:09:09.803
Starting in the 1970s, right-wing extremists repackaged the old ideology of Aryan racism, elitism, and force.

00:09:09.803 --> 00:09:46.240
They used new cultic forms that mixed esotericism and Eastern religions. In Austria and Germany, former SS man Wilhelm Landig revived the ariosophical mythology of Thule. Thule was the supposed polar homeland of the ancient Aryans. He created the idea of the Black Sun. This was a substitute swastika and a mystical energy source that could regenerate the Aryan race. He popularized esoteric ideas found in the pre-Nazi völkisch movement and the SS.

00:09:46.240 --> 00:09:55.456
These ideas covered Atlantis, the World Ice Theory, prehistoric floods, and secret racial doctrines from Tibet.

00:09:55.456 --> 00:10:25.749
He also highlighted Nazi interest in the medieval Cathars and Grail traditions. He presented these as an alternative Germanic religion of dualist heresy. In Italy, Julius Evola's aristocratic elitism and esoteric Aryan-Nordic traditions inspired a whole generation of postwar neo-fascists. When wanted far-right terrorists fled abroad, they carried Evola's ideas to far-right parties and groups elsewhere in Europe.

00:10:25.749 --> 00:10:58.603
By the late 1980s, this little-known philosopher had become a major political icon of opposition to democracy and liberalism in the West. Julius Evola's interest in the Indo-Aryan world included the exotic realms of Hinduism and Tantrism. Following James Madole's early adoption of Theosophy and Hindu caste hierarchies, neo-Nazi ideology absorbed Eastern themes in the mystical doctrines of Savitri Devi and Miguel Serrano.

00:10:58.603 --> 00:11:31.115
These two are currently popular in the racist underground. Savitri Devi, a French-born Nazi-Hindu prophetess, described Hitler as an avatar of Vishnu. She compared Nazism to the cult of Shiva, which emphasizes destruction and new creation. Adopting the Hindu cycle of the ages, she claimed that mankind is living in the Kali Yuga, a dismal dark age. She argued that only regenerative violence, war, and genocide can end it.

00:11:31.115 --> 00:11:43.659
Miguel Serrano, a retired Chilean diplomat and author, blends exotic oriental religion with his Gnostic-Manichaean doctrine of "Esoteric Hitlerism."

00:11:43.659 --> 00:12:21.803
Serrano traces the semi-divine Aryans to extraterrestrial origins. He recommends kundalini yoga to repurify "mystical Aryan blood" to its former quality of divine light. His other themes include a Gnostic war against the Jews, the Black Sun, the Hitler avatar, and Nazi UFOs in Antarctica. Neo-Nazism has thereby acquired new myths and meanings for a younger generation. Another revaluation of Nazism came from its demonization in many thrillers and books about Nazi occultism.

00:12:21.803 --> 00:12:55.424
These were published in sensational paperback editions during the 1960s and 1970s. In these works, Nazism was mystified and romanticized into a neo-Gnostic religion. It had links to oriental mythology, secret Tibetan doctrines, and demonic inspiration. This effect turned the facts of dictatorship, terror, war, and oppression into a mythological tableau. It removed them from history. Reality soon followed popular literature.

00:12:55.424 --> 00:13:28.533
In the early 1970s, satanist groups in the United States flirted with Nazi themes. They saw these themes as symbols of the forbidden, dark side of life. In the 1990s, Nazi satanic cults replaced these experiments in the shock value of Nazism. These cults linked anti-Christian paganism to a transgressive praise of Hitler and the Third Reich. In America, Europe, and Australia, such "darkside" lodges espouse a vulgar Nietzschean worship of force.

00:13:28.533 --> 00:13:40.480
They back this with anti-Christian, elitist, and Social Darwinist doctrines. In the 1980s and 1990s, the far right saw a dramatic revival in Europe and America.

00:13:40.480 --> 00:14:11.371
This was especially true among alienated white youth and lower-income groups. These groups felt increasingly pushed aside by new high-tech industries. They also felt marginalized by the growing presence of ethnic minorities in their communities. Rapid growth in Hispanic and Third World immigration in the United States fueled fresh fears of racial inundation. Similar immigration from developing countries into Western Europe had the same effect.

00:14:11.371 --> 00:14:43.541
The collapse of the Soviet Union and Yugoslavia led to further migrations. Gypsies and East European nationals moved to Western Europe. Free-trade agreements, the collapse of traditional manufacturing, and the export of service jobs abroad via computer communications are stimulating racism and hostility toward liberalism. Globalization is sending huge flows of capital, information, skills, and people across national borders.

00:14:43.541 --> 00:15:17.163
The Western world is quickly going through major structural changes. Borders are becoming easier to cross. Skilled workers, economic migrants, refugees, and asylum seekers are moving into advanced industrial countries in growing numbers. As more immigrant groups arrive, traditional national culture faces unfamiliar customs, norms, and religions. At the start of our new century, these cultural trends put great pressure on the idea of the nation-state.

00:15:17.163 --> 00:15:50.528
A century later, liberalism and laissez-faire capitalism are again seen as the engines of unwanted and threatening change. Once again, extremist nationalist reactions echo völkisch ideas. They focus on defensive race ideologies to counter threats to national and cultural identity. Some challenged groups turn to racial identity as a last resort. In the United States, the doctrine of Christian Identity mixes heretical Christian dualism with a vicious anti-Semitic theology.

00:15:50.528 --> 00:16:27.648
This theology views Jews as the "spawn of Satan." It stigmatizes African Americans, Asians, Hispanics, and all other colored peoples as "mud" races. These groups claim these peoples are diluting and destroying the Aryan race in its traditional white homelands. Here, Nazi demonology and apocalyptic ideas are freely invoked. They are combined with Hitler worship and Third Reich symbolism. This mobilizes violence to support a white racial state. Other groups mix racism with Nordic pagan religions.

00:16:27.648 --> 00:17:02.293
They celebrate runes as magical signs of ancestral heritage and mystical blood loyalty. In the United States, Britain, Germany, and the Scandinavian countries, racial pagan groups study runes, magic, and the sinister mythology of the Norse gods Wotan, Loki, and Fenriswolf. The racial interpretation of these esoteric ideas, cosmology, and prophecies reveals these groups' overwhelming anxiety about the future of white identity in multiracial societies.

00:17:02.293 --> 00:17:36.427
This book began as a sequel to The Occult Roots of Nazism. It aimed to document how occult Nazi themes survived after the war. As I worked, my view widened greatly. I did not just trace faded fascist mystics and outdated ideas. I actually wrote a new history of modern neo-völkisch groups and ideas in America and Europe. This new völkisch revival is common in the English-speaking world. It shows a reaction to the rise of liberalism and globalization from the 1980s onward.

00:17:36.427 --> 00:17:44.107
The original völkisch movement started as a defense of German identity against modernity in the late 1800s.

00:17:44.107 --> 00:18:23.360
This neo-völkisch revival does the same for white identity. It defends against multiculturalism, affirmative action, and mass immigration from the Third World. As these neo-völkisch groups focus on identity and ethnicity, many turn to esoteric themes. They explore Aryan origins, secret knowledge, and occult heritage. Their German predecessors did the same. Like the Ariosophists from 1890 to 1945, these new white-pride movements are the most radical response.

00:18:23.360 --> 00:18:57.664
Western societies now face deep challenges to their cultural identity. The original völkisch movement led to National Socialism and the Third Reich. So, the rise of a new völkisch movement should worry us. Who knows what politics and societies will emerge by 2030-50 from the growing sense of white marginalization? I know this provocative study of modern racist movements may offend politically correct views. It asks questions that liberal elites prefer to ignore or suppress.

00:18:57.664 --> 00:19:12.853
Racist religion carries great risks. When people project their grievances, fears, and anxieties onto "shadow" figures of other races, religious transcendence is stunted and twisted into exclusion and hatred.

00:19:12.853 --> 00:19:48.949
Instead of genuine spirituality, we see partiality, separation, and restriction. A rigid self-righteousness leads into the spiritual basement of primitive dualism, where pseudo-salvation depends on eliminating the Other. Projecting religious Manichaeism onto human differences inevitably causes strife and violence. Whenever human groups are viewed as absolute categories of good and evil, light and darkness, both the human community and humanity itself are diminished.

00:19:48.949 --> 00:20:04.651
Such degraded religion never leads to light, only to darkness. I hope that understanding the substitute faiths documented in these pages, along with their causes, can help us avoid repeating past conflagrations.

00:20:04.651 --> 00:20:04.751


00:20:04.751 --> 00:20:22.756
1. American Neo-Nazism. American neo-Nazism is an exotic import from Europe that has always gone beyond American nationalism. American neo-Nazis see themselves as brothers to all white men in a global movement of racial nationalism.

00:20:22.756 --> 00:20:56.121
They remain fixated on Adolf Hitler as the lost savior of the Western world. Yet his German nationalist limits are replaced by their wider vision of a pan-Aryan movement. In this vision, the United States leads as the top white power in the postwar world. American neo-Nazism traces its roots to the early 1950s. At that time, the anti-communist ideology of the Cold War found a nostalgic model in Hitler's attempt to destroy the Soviet Union.

00:20:56.121 --> 00:21:30.340
Neo-Nazism quickly labeled liberalism and American Jews as the helpers of communism. This created a violent anti-Semitism based on Nazi models. However, desegregation and the black civil rights movement of the early 1960s provided the lasting political drive for American racial nationalism. The social empowerment of black Americans, forced integration, busing, affirmative action, and equal opportunities led American neo-Nazis to take on a white supremacist role.

00:21:30.340 --> 00:21:42.201
When large-scale Hispanic and other Third World immigration began in the 1980s, American neo-Nazism saw itself as the front-line defense of America's survival as a white nation.

00:21:42.201 --> 00:22:11.812
The changing ethnic mix of the United States is a deep issue. So is the political unity of an increasingly diverse multicultural society. The path of American neo-Nazism from George Lincoln Rockwell in the 1960s to William Pierce in the 2000s shows how the religious myths of German National Socialism apply to major cultural changes in American demography and identity.

00:22:11.812 --> 00:22:39.801
George Lincoln Rockwell, who called himself the Führer of the 1960s, is always identified as the founder of the openly pro-Hitler, postwar Nazi movement in the United States. Rockwell's extravagant praise for Hitler, his violent racism against Jews and blacks, and his use of excess and exhibitionist tactics have given him a lasting place in the folklore of American political extremism.

00:22:39.801 --> 00:23:06.169
Disappointed by his earlier political work with old-style far-right groups, Rockwell founded his American Nazi Party in 1959. He adopted a brazen Nazi image, complete with swastika flags, stormtroopers, and open declarations of his intention to gas the Jews. He fantasized that he would become president of the United States by 1973.

00:23:06.169 --> 00:23:37.572
He imagined that a Senate and House of Representatives made up of his party's members would support him. His political program was firmly grounded in a policy of "white survival." This policy aimed at the wholesale repatriation of all American Negroes to Africa and the extermination of the Jews. He regarded the Jews as the architects of racial desegregation, national decline, and cultural degeneracy. Rockwell's public appearances mixed clowning with provocation.

00:23:37.572 --> 00:23:56.260
Soon after founding the party, Rockwell and his men regularly picketed the White House. They held signs that read "Save Ike from the kikes," "The only communist party in the Middle East is in Israel," "Gas red Jewish spies," and "Communism is Jewish."

00:23:56.260 --> 00:24:31.759
In 1961, Rockwell drove a "Hate Bus" through the South. His party was arrested in New Orleans. The bus sides displayed notices like "We do hate race-mixing" and "We hate Jew-Communism." Back in Washington, his stormtroopers drove a bus around the city. It bore the slogan: "Rockwell is right! Who needs niggers?" In Boston and Philadelphia, the party picketed cinemas showing the popular film Exodus, which told the story of Jewish immigrants to Israel after World War II.

00:24:31.759 --> 00:25:02.649
They held banners demanding "America for Whites and Gas Chamber for Traitors." Throughout the mid-1960s, Rockwell and his American Nazi Party took part in many protests and disruptions. Charges against stormtroopers included fighting, loitering, vagrancy, and assault. They also faced charges of desertion, criminal defamation, and unlawful possession of firearms. What makes an American Nazi?

00:25:02.649 --> 00:25:40.452
Looking at Rockwell's life, we see a mix of religious belief and idealism. These drove a loud program of anti-Semitism and anti-communism, white supremacy, and eugenics. His showy tactics likely came from his parents' background. George Lincoln Rockwell was born on 9 March 1918 in Bloomington, Illinois. He was the eldest son of theatrical performers. His father, George Lovejoy "Doc" Rockwell, was a vaudeville comedian. He had English and Scottish ancestry.

00:25:40.452 --> 00:26:09.807
He had a top act on Broadway. He was well known on radio and in the leading theaters of the country. His mother, born Claire Schade, was a young German-French toe dancer. She was part of a family dance team. After his parents divorced, he spent his childhood staying with his mother in rural Illinois. He also stayed with his father on the Maine coast. Regular house guests included Fred Allen, Benny Goodman, and Groucho Marx.

00:26:09.807 --> 00:26:36.431
After finishing prep school at Hebron Academy, Rockwell went to Brown University in 1938 to study philosophy and sociology. He soon turned against the liberal, egalitarian tone of social science and his teachers. Later, he believed that liberalism was the "pimping little sister" of communism. His grades were poor, but he served as art editor for the campus magazine, Sir Brown.

00:26:36.431 --> 00:27:12.356
His cartoons ranged from humor to comic book horror, featuring images of violence, destruction, and bombings. The prospect of war offered a welcome break from his studies. Eager for action, high-strung, and edgy, Rockwell was influenced by the growing anti-German sentiment. By March 1941, he had enlisted in the Naval Air Corps and quickly earned his wings. He served as a naval aviator flying anti-submarine missions in the South Atlantic and South Pacific throughout World War II.

00:27:12.356 --> 00:27:31.215
He commanded naval air support at the Battle of Guadalcanal and during the invasion of Guam in August 1944. He was discharged in October 1945 with the rank of lieutenant commander and several decorations. Meanwhile, he married a girl he had known as a student at Brown.

00:27:31.215 --> 00:28:03.044
After leaving the navy, Rockwell spent the first five years studying art. He then took various jobs as a commercial photographer, a painter, an advertising executive, and a publisher in Maine and New York. He showed some promise as a commercial artist and enrolled at the Pratt Institute in New York. In 1948, he won a $1,000 prize in a national art contest sponsored by the National Society of Illustrators. But war interrupted his career again.

00:28:03.044 --> 00:28:31.716
In 1950, when the Korean War began, Rockwell returned to active duty. He trained fighter pilots in southern California. His involvement in the Korean conflict created in him a lasting hatred of communism. It also bred a paranoid fear that communism would undermine the United States. Rockwell first became politically involved here in the campaign to elect military hero General Douglas MacArthur as president.

00:28:31.716 --> 00:28:59.620
Joseph McCarthy's anti-communist revelations also dominated this time. Rockwell deeply suspected the motives of those trying to discredit him. An old lady in San Diego who worked on the MacArthur campaign showed him some newspapers. She claimed Jews controlled these papers and used them to smear both men. She introduced him to McCarthy's speeches and Conde McGinley's anti-Semitic newspaper, Common Sense,.

00:28:59.620 --> 00:29:31.705
This paper contained shocking claims about a secret Jewish-communist plot behind the scenes of twentieth-century history. She also encouraged him to attend a speech by veteran anti-Semite and rabble-rouser Gerald L. K. Smith in Los Angeles. Rockwell was overwhelmed by Smith's emotional exposure of the Jewish conspiracy and its bid for world power. Through further reading in the San Diego public library, he became convinced that a Jewish-communist world conspiracy existed.

00:29:31.705 --> 00:29:48.601
Rockwell was staggered by both the apparent size of the conspiracy and the silence of officials and media about it. One autumn day in 1950, in the dark book stacks of the San Diego library, Rockwell experienced illumination and political awakening.

00:29:48.601 --> 00:30:21.369
He had always felt that the world was out of joint and that mischief was afoot. But now he felt he held the key to the past and the present. Yet how could he fight against this monstrous and universal plot? Given the apparent enormity of the Jewish world conspiracy, Rockwell now wondered why America had gone to war on the side of the communist Soviet Union. He opposed "Christian Germany, which never had a single highly placed spy in [America], and no plans for conquering the world."

00:30:21.369 --> 00:30:47.652
The example of Adolf Hitler and his crusade against world Jewry and communism quickly came to mind. Rockwell believed Hitler had understood the Jewish menace from the outset of his career. He believed the Jews had involved Britain and America in the conflict for their own interests. Early in 1951, Rockwell found a copy of Mein Kampf in a local bookshop. He read it and saw the world anew:

00:30:47.652 --> 00:31:04.975
I found abundant "mental sunshine," which suddenly bathed the gray world in the clear light of reason and understanding. Word after word, sentence after sentence, stabbed into the darkness like thunderclaps and lightningbolts of revelation.

00:31:04.975 --> 00:31:41.412
They tore and ripped away the cobwebs of more than thirty years of darkness. They brilliantly illuminated the mysteries of the heretofore impenetrable murk in a world gone mad. I was transfixed, hypnotized. I wondered at the utter, indescribable genius of it. I realized that National Socialism, the iconoclastic world view of Adolf Hitler, was the doctrine of scientific racial idealism. It was actually a new religion. George Lincoln Rockwell converted to National Socialism.

00:31:41.412 --> 00:32:03.513
In later years, he wrote that future generations would see Adolf Hitler as the White Savior of the twentieth century. He also said they would view the Fuehrerbunker in Berlin as the Alamo of the White race. It took another eight years before he became a vocal Hitler supporter leading the American Nazi Party.

00:32:03.513 --> 00:32:32.868
In November 1952, the navy sent him to a base at Keflavik in Iceland. He spent two years there as an F8F Bearcat pilot and reached the rank of commander. He met his second wife, Thora Hallgrimsson, there. She came from a prominent local family and was the niece of Iceland's ambassador to the United States. Rockwell was still deeply absorbed in Mein Kampf. He took his bride to Berchtesgaden, Germany, for their honeymoon.

00:32:32.868 --> 00:33:02.137
They visited Hitler's Eagle's Nest with feelings of reverence and fascination. After returning to civilian life, he decided to enter magazine publishing. He hoped to find a living and a place to share his political ideas. He was also active in right-wing groups. He tried to start an American Federation of Conservative Organizations. He tried to move forward by hiding his core Nazi beliefs behind a respectable front. Eventually, he gave up on this strategy.

00:33:02.137 --> 00:33:14.511
It failed to attract dedicated racists and anti-Semites. In the winter of 1957-58, Rockwell had a series of recurring dreams that always ended with him meeting Hitler.

00:33:14.511 --> 00:33:43.780
This prompted him to go public against what he saw as Jewish power in America. He received financial support from Harold N. Arrowsmith, a wealthy anti-Semite. In Arlington, Virginia, they formed the National Committee to Free America from Jewish Domination. After a maverick campaign for the governorship of Georgia, Rockwell's first chance for confrontation came in May 1958. The U.S. government provided military aid to the Chamoun regime in Lebanon.

00:33:43.780 --> 00:34:14.159
This aid was unpopular with Lebanese Arabs but enjoyed the support of the Israelis. On 29 July 1958, Rockwell led a picket of the White House. He protested against Jewish influence on the government. He also organized simultaneous demonstrations in Atlanta, Georgia, and Louisville, Kentucky. Earlier that year, Rockwell had helped found the National States Rights Party. This was a new anti-Semitic and racist party in Georgia.

00:34:14.159 --> 00:34:41.124
On 12 October, a synagogue in Atlanta was blown up. The police seized Rockwell's supporters there. Newspapers around the world carried stories implicating Rockwell. Now he and his family were harassed, and his home was attacked. Arrowsmith retreated from the glare of the publicity and withdrew his support. His wife and children soon found the strain too great and returned to Iceland.

00:34:41.124 --> 00:35:15.172
Rockwell was left alone by his family and former supporters. He faced a bleak and solitary future in the early months of 1959. One cold March morning in his house at Arlington, he sat alone with a huge swastika banner and a plaque of Hitler. After another "religious experience" that involved a brief state of universal awareness, he became convinced he had to fulfill Hitler's mission. This meant achieving a total, global victory over the forces of tyranny and oppression.

00:35:15.172 --> 00:35:26.777
He would become an overt National Socialist and a self-proclaimed devotee of Hitler. He abandoned all thought of working with conservative groups or maintaining respectability.

00:35:26.777 --> 00:36:00.313
He proudly displayed his Nazi banner. He recruited a handful of stormtroopers. He issued them grayshirt uniforms and swastika armbands. He mounted a large illuminated swastika on the roof of his house. He founded the American Party, later called the American Nazi Party. Besides the party headquarters at his house at 2507 North Franklin Road in Arlington, Rockwell also maintained a barracks in a run-down farmhouse nearby.

00:36:00.313 --> 00:36:13.625
This housed his growing detachment of stormtroopers. After Rockwell chose to openly declare his support for Nazism, he focused all his actions on provoking Jews and society at all.

00:36:13.625 --> 00:36:48.100
He saw society as a passive victim. He and his stormtroopers showed off their Nazi uniforms and badges. They missed no chance to shock and anger the public. Starting in 1960, his bold and sensational acts aimed to get maximum press coverage. This was for a fringe group that was considered crazy by others. The group had no more than two hundred members at its peak. Rockwell gave speeches to curious crowds and eager reporters. He stood surrounded by waving American and swastika flags.

00:36:48.100 --> 00:37:23.001
He pushed a national and then global plan for eugenics to purify the Aryan race. He constantly called Jews the representatives of Marxism, unchecked capitalism, racial decay, and cultural Bolshevism. He demanded that they be tried and killed by gas. Rockwell forced the media to cover him. He did this by distributing inflammatory leaflets, causing public incidents, and yelling at crowds to provoke violent reactions. The American Nazi Party also had a racist policy toward Black people.

00:37:23.001 --> 00:37:52.697
Rockwell rejected all race mixing and desegregation. He called them Jewish tricks to mix the American racial stock. He proposed moving all American Black people to a new African state. The U.S. government would fund this. On 25 February 1962, he spoke as a guest at a major Black Muslim convention in Chicago. He told an audience of more than twelve thousand people that he saw Elijah Muhammad as the Adolf Hitler of Black people.

00:37:52.697 --> 00:38:22.308
In private, Rockwell imagined that this deportation plan would follow an upcoming race war and the mass killing of Black people. Rockwell's rise to fame depended heavily on the growing strength of the civil rights movement among American blacks, led by Martin Luther King Jr. In the early 1960s, Black people became more politically aware. Protests, marches, and the Watts and Harlem riots showed their impatience for true equality in American society.

00:38:22.308 --> 00:38:54.735
This was a time when liberals worried about the plight of Black people. Measures to end segregation were put in place, and busing white and Black children to mixed schools became common. Rockwell hated all of this. He viewed Black people as a primitive, lazy race who wanted only simple pleasures and a life of irresponsibility. He believed they had been content as slaves, but their problems started after they became more involved in the social and economic life of white people.

00:38:54.735 --> 00:39:16.751
Rockwell was convinced that Jews had pushed Black people into a hopeless position of supposed equality with whites. Deeply frustrated by their inability to compete in education and for jobs, Black people had become violent. This fulfilled Jewish plans to stir up the breakdown of the traditional order and the rise of communism.

00:39:16.751 --> 00:39:47.385
By constantly emphasizing the threat of increasing Black riots, and combining this with his intense anti-Semitism and anti-communism, Rockwell tried to exploit deep American fears about the apparent disorder of the 1960s. The American Nazi Party carried out a steady stream of protests and disruptions during this period. Jewish youths were beaten, a synagogue in Bridgeport, Connecticut, was bombed, and the word "Jew" was painted on front doors.

00:39:47.385 --> 00:40:03.172
In early 1962, Rockwell began planning a large rally to celebrate Hitler's birthday in April. That summer, he attended an international Nazi camp congress in Gloucestershire, organized by British neo-Nazi leader Colin Jordan.

00:40:03.172 --> 00:40:32.783
Jordan held the event despite a Home Office ban on his entry to Britain. The group agreed to found a World Union of National Socialists. After his deportation back to the United States, Rockwell picketed the White House in protest. In September 1962, he gave one of his captains, Roy James, a medal for punching Martin Luther King Jr. in the face in Birmingham, Alabama. Several disruptive incidents also occurred in the House of Representatives.

00:40:32.783 --> 00:41:04.441
One involved Robert A. Lloyd, who ran into the proceedings wearing blackface and a stovepipe hat. He shouted "Long live Rockwell" and asked to be seated as a Mississippi congressman, mimicking a Black person's speech. Rockwell himself was charged with disorderly conduct and stood trial in New York in June 1966. A Jewish lawyer defended him. The court acquitted Rockwell by upholding the free speech rights he denied to his enemies.

00:41:04.441 --> 00:41:15.023
While American groups made headlines, Rockwell tried to give the World Union of National Socialists (WUNS) a philosophical basis.

00:41:15.023 --> 00:41:48.729
The WUNS was a federation of about seven national Nazi groups and parties. These groups were in Britain, the United States, Chile, Denmark, France, Argentina, and Australia. Colin Jordan originally led the WUNS when it formed in August 1962. Later that year, Jordan went to prison for public order offenses. Rockwell then took over the leadership. Through the WUNS, Rockwell wanted to show that National Socialism's racial idealism was a program for global Aryan power.

00:41:48.729 --> 00:42:19.620
He wanted to place this above the nationalisms of the past. He aimed this message at a younger generation of new supporters. Rockwell believed this ideology was necessary to counter the Jewish world conspiracy. He also believed it was needed to counter the rising tide of colored peoples around the planet. In the spring of 1966, Rockwell started publishing a new WUNS periodical called National Socialist World. He published it from his headquarters in Arlington.

00:42:19.620 --> 00:42:30.799
This was a new forum for international Nazi ideology. Rockwell appointed Dr. William Luther Pierce (b. 1933) as editor.

00:42:30.799 --> 00:43:03.908
Pierce was new to the neo-Nazi movement. He was a physicist. He studied at Rice University and the California Institute of Technology. He completed his doctorate at the University of Colorado. He then taught at Oregon State University for three years. From the start, National Socialist World built its image as the leading international Nazi periodical. It featured long articles and book reviews. These pieces were ostensibly written for an educated, literate readership.

00:43:03.908 --> 00:43:36.164
The magazine used high production standards. It was intended to be a quarterly. Each issue had over a hundred pages. The first issue included a philosophical appraisal of National Socialism by Colin Jordan. It also included an article by George Lincoln Rockwell on the value of vulgar Nazi propaganda. A condensed edition of The Lightning and the Sun by Savitri Devi took pride of place. Savitri Devi was a Hindu-Nordicist.

00:43:36.164 --> 00:44:09.785
Her Hitler cult and philosophy of history deeply influenced neo-Nazi intellectuals (see chapter 5). By the winter of 1968, six issues had been published. These covered topics such as Gottfried Feder's twenty-five points of the German Nazi Party. They also included Matt Koehl on Hitler and National Socialist doctrine. And they featured Robert F. Williams on race war in America. The magazine promoted the memory of Hitler and the Third Reich in its articles and book reviews.

00:44:09.785 --> 00:44:40.932
It also stressed the future role of the United States in the coming global racial struggle. In a long editorial for the summer 1967 issue, Pierce listed the forces in a war of dominance and survival. He named "150 million more-or-less Aryan whites, 25 million Negroes and 6 million Jews." He claimed that Jewish control of public opinion, finance, and education hid the core of this conflict.

00:44:40.932 --> 00:45:15.919
He predicted that disorders would increase for the time being. He said that all Negro arson, murder, and insurrection would still be blamed on poverty and discrimination. People would also blame white prejudice and bigotry, police brutality, and injustice. Welfare bribes and leniency toward blacks would grow. Preachers would call for more tolerance. Meanwhile, America would descend into an inferno. He expected that active National Socialists would soon be outlawed.

00:45:15.919 --> 00:45:46.639
They would be forced into illegal, underground activities. Nevertheless, Pierce ultimately hoped for a specific outcome. He wrote that "once Aryan America has become racially self-conscious, has organised itself, flexed its muscles, and scented blood, the Jews will follow the Negroes into history's garbage pail in short order." Rockwell saw the limits of a movement focused only on publicity stunts and provocation.

00:45:46.639 --> 00:46:23.076
He began planning a longer-term strategy for the party. This strategy involved mass organization and electoral campaigning. On 1 January 1967, the party changed its name to the National Socialist White Peoples' Party (NSWPP). A party conference in June dealt with fund-raising, propaganda writing, and membership recruitment. But these plans ended abruptly. On 25 August 1967, Rockwell was shot by a sniper. He was reversing his vehicle out of a parking lot.

00:46:23.076 --> 00:46:55.759
He had just left a laundromat in Arlington. The assassin was John Patler. Patler had edited the party bulletin, The Stormtrooper. He had worked with the National Renaissance Party and Rockwell's American Nazi Party. He then left to start his own group, the American National Party. That group lasted from 1962 to early 1963. Patler later returned to join Rockwell. But he caused friction because of his unstable character and Marxist leanings.

00:46:55.759 --> 00:47:17.860
In March 1967, Rockwell expelled him from the party. The reason was that Patler was stirring up dissent between fair and dark-skinned members. Patler was tried for murder. He was found guilty. He was sentenced to twenty years in prison. Rockwell's death gave the U.S. Nazi movement a martyr.

00:47:17.860 --> 00:47:52.761
It soon split into several small extremist political groups. These groups were driven by fanaticism, paranoia, and suspicion. The NSWPP had about five hundred members. They split into various factions. Matt Koehl was Rockwell's chief lieutenant and formal successor. He had been a party member since 1963. Koehl kept the party name and the Arlington headquarters. He had the largest following. One schismatic group in California formally re-adopted the American Nazi Party title.

00:47:52.761 --> 00:48:18.105
James Warner first led this group. He had been secretary of the parent party in the early 1960s. The other major heirs of Rockwell's party were the National Socialist Liberation Front, the National Socialist Party of America, the National Alliance, and the Christian Defense League. Matthias Koehl Jr. was born on 22 January 1935 in Milwaukee, Wisconsin.

00:48:18.105 --> 00:48:45.924
His parents were Hungarian immigrants of German descent. He studied journalism at the University of Wisconsin. Then he enlisted in the U.S. Marine Corps and served two years on active duty. As a schoolboy, Matt Koehl was drawn to anti-Semitism. In New York City, he joined James Madole's National Renaissance Party. In 1957, he helped organize the United White Party in Knoxville, Tennessee.

00:48:45.924 --> 00:48:53.689
By 1958, he was the national organizer of the National States' Rights Party (NSRP).

00:48:53.689 --> 00:49:24.068
This group agitated against desegregation in the southern states. In 1960, he joined Rockwell's movement. In 1961, he became leader of the Chicago section. In 1963, he joined Rockwell at party headquarters in Arlington. He was appointed corresponding secretary of the WUNS and national secretary of the NSWPP. He also edited and published both the WUNS Bulletin and the party's NS Bulletin.

00:49:24.068 --> 00:49:57.092
His attraction to the American Nazi Party came from pride in his German origins. He also admired Adolf Hitler with a devotion bordering on religious adulation. In an early article for National Socialist World, Koehl praised Hitler as an idealist, a visionary, and the creator of a heroic new worldview. He described Hitler as someone who worked for a broad Aryan racial revival beyond the limits of German nationalism. This idea was inspired by the pan-Aryan Savitri Devi.

00:49:57.092 --> 00:50:16.377
His swastika was intended to represent "the mission of the struggle for the victory of Aryan man" and a New Order of racial blood-brotherhood. In 1968, Koehl stated that "Adolf Hitler is National Socialism, just as National Socialism is Adolf Hitler."

00:50:16.377 --> 00:50:48.121
He described Nazi ideology as a creed and a new faith. He rejected the view that American Nazis were fighting for a historical German phenomenon. These critics had failed to understand "the Truth which Adolf Hitler revealed to the world nearly 50 years ago.… Our goal involves far more than the realization of some superficial political or social scheme. It entails a universal transformation of ideas and things, an upheaval of unprecedented magnitude."

00:50:48.121 --> 00:51:14.660
Koehl was impressed by Hitler's claim that humans can live only by higher ideals. He quoted a long passage from Mein Kampf. That passage claimed "the [National Socialist] philosophy of life corresponds to the innermost will of Nature,… until at last the best of mankind, having achieved possession of this earth, will have a free path for activity in domains [beyond]."

00:51:14.660 --> 00:51:30.617
Koehl's full-blown Hitler cult is even clearer in the New Order, the name his party took after a general reorganization in 1983. Its literature says the group has about two hundred full members and four hundred active supporters.

00:51:30.617 --> 00:52:08.761
These people are organized into some forty local branches across eighteen states, from California to the East Coast. Regular activities include celebrating Hitler's birthday. They also hold lectures and seminars to spread the Nazi gospel. Matt Koehl's own speeches to U.S. groups and his occasional trips to European neo-Nazi gatherings set out the "racial idealism" of modern Hitlerism. His books The Future Calls (1972) and Faith of the Future (1995) do the same.

00:52:08.761 --> 00:52:43.577
They use strong, evangelical prose aimed at all new recruits and initiates of the New Order. New Order literature, distributed from its Milwaukee headquarters, includes small votive pictures of Hitler with the caption "He lives!" Another small card carries the text "Our Creed" in English and an overleaf in German. The self-conscious imitation of Christian liturgy and belief, implicit in its blasphemous substitution of Hitler for Jesus Christ, comes close to parody: We believe in Adolf Hitler,

00:52:43.577 --> 00:53:07.641
the immortal Leader of our race, singular gift of Providence, greatest figure of all time, alive in our hearts today and forever. We believe in his holy Cause, which is the New Order, the fulfillment of Aryan destiny. in accordance with the eternal laws of life, the hope and future of our kind on earth.

00:53:07.641 --> 00:53:21.721
We believe in his Movement, the true, undivided body of his followers, which bears the name of his Cause. as the instrument of his will, consecrated by the blood of heroes and martyrs.

00:53:21.721 --> 00:53:33.327
- the only way to world redemption. HEIL HITLER! In his writings and speeches to New Order audiences, Matt Koehl often uses religious myths and symbols.

00:53:33.327 --> 00:54:06.436
Savitri Devi's Hindu-Aryan ideas and nature worship strongly shape these passages. In a piece called "Resurrection," written for Hitler's birthday in April 1987, Koehl recalled words from the Bhagavad-Gita. Savitri Devi called this text an "ancient book of Aryan wisdom and insight." It says: "Age after age, when justice is crushed, when evil reigns supreme, I come; again am I born on Earth to save the world."

00:54:06.436 --> 00:54:46.628
Mixing Hindu, pagan, and Christian themes, Koehl reflected on Nature's endless message of renewal and resurrection. He wrote: "Adolf Hitler was born on Earth. He became flesh and blood. He fought, and he died." Koehl claimed that Hitler had to die. He said Hitler's death was a necessary fate. The tragic events of 1945 were a dramatic sign of a new world to come. He wrote: "Hitler lives in our very own hearts and minds.… Our Leader is risen. He is risen indeed!"

00:54:46.628 --> 00:54:58.745
In a 1991 speech to a gathering of Dutch, Flemish, and German New Order members in Europe, Koehl compared the end of World War II to the start of a new era.

00:54:58.745 --> 00:55:30.319
He likened postwar Hitlerism to the early spread of Christianity. This new faith seemed defeated after Jesus was crucified in A.D. 33 and his followers were scattered and persecuted. Yet Calvary marked Christ's final victory, in which Christians had full confidence. Using a vulgar metaphor, Koehl called the later victory of the faith the Christian Endsieg and asked if modern Nazis share that same drive to win. The length of the struggle does not matter.

00:55:30.319 --> 00:56:00.697
Only unshakable faith can sustain them. "We can make a start … and whether it takes 50 years, 100 years, 500 years or 1,000 years, the important thing is that one day - sooner or later - the cause of Adolf Hitler does indeed prevail on this earth." Koehl rejected Christianity as a foreign Semitic faith. Yet he used religious symbols that are clearly Christian to express New Order doctrine.

00:56:00.697 --> 00:56:36.196
He presented Hitler as the messiah of Aryan salvation. He wrote, "He is our law and guide as Aryans for all time to come. He is our hope, our redemption." He spoke of Hitler's "transfiguration" and the gathering of a "sacred retinue." Koehl's use of redemptive symbolism is often overwhelming. He wrote, "As the darkness of dying civilization casts its lengthening shadow over a confused and despairing world, the faith of the future will shine forth …

00:56:36.196 --> 00:57:08.537
a resplendent New Order …guided and instructed by the immortal personality of the greatest figure ever to walk the face of this earth." It is hard to find a more fervent expression of Hitler worship than these messianic and apocalyptic outpourings, which are obviously taken from Christian models. The New Order's sectarian nature is also clear in its fierce rejection of the modern liberal world, which it equates with unchecked license, moral decline, and physical disease.

00:57:08.537 --> 00:57:34.393
Koehl asks what kind of world the victors of 1945 actually gave us, if we judge Hitler by the standards of his democratic opponents. What is the cultural and political record of the Allies without Hitler after fifty years? Koehl sees a world of rat-race consumerism, self-fixation, environmental devastation, pollution, and race mixing.

00:57:34.393 --> 00:57:48.815
"They altered the national demography and introduced us to integration, busing, Affirmative Action, minority quotas, sensitivity training, Black History and - the Holocaust.

00:57:48.815 --> 00:58:29.689
They gave us permissiveness, drugs, MTV and teen suicide. They gave us safe sex and unsafe streets and gun control. They gave us rock 'n roll and rape-counseling centers. They gave us 'alternative lifestyles,' sodomy, AIDS, filth, perversion, chaos, crime, corruption, dumbing down and insanity of every kind." This overwhelming cultural pessimism is used to condemn the modern world as the final gasp of an old order following its temporary defeat of Hitler and National Socialism.

00:58:29.689 --> 00:58:51.791
While Koehl was building a church, another NSWPP faction embraced outright terrorism. Joseph Charles Tommasi (b. 1951) was a young leader of the NSWPP in southern California. In 1974, he founded the National Socialist Liberation Front (NSLF).

00:58:51.791 --> 00:59:23.791
Tommasi broke with the "straight" conservative image of American Nazism. He grew his hair long and smoked marijuana. Copying the militant left, Tommasi called for an armed guerrilla struggle against the "Jewish power structure" of the United States. One famous NSLF poster read: "The future belongs to the few of us still willing to get our hands dirty." Along the barrel of a cocked gun ran the words "Political terror. It's the only thing they understand."

00:59:23.791 --> 00:59:58.692
Tommasi denied all interest in law and order. He wanted anarchy and chaos so that the NSLF could attack the "System" and its hated police protectors. NSLF armaments guidelines included magnum shotguns, 45-caliber automatic pistols and semiautomatic military assault rifles. Propaganda pictures showed the twisted wreckage of a bombed-out Bank of America branch. The cover photograph of the NSLF periodical, Siege, showed the ruins of another terrorist target.

00:59:58.692 --> 01:00:28.047
This image was incidentally taken from the radical left-wing Students for a Democratic Society (SDS). The NSLF's call for armed struggle was not matched for another decade, until the terrorist attacks by The Order or Brüders Schweigen in the mid-1980s. In 1980, James N. Mason (born 1952), a violent Nazi who had joined Rockwell in the mid-1960s, revived the NSLF.

01:00:28.047 --> 01:01:01.327
The group had lapsed after Tommasi's assassination in 1975. Mason restarted it as a forerunner for new militant American white supremacist movements. These groups were committed to an armed struggle against the so-called Zionist Occupation Government (ZOG). This is a current far-right term for the U.S. government as a Jewish-controlled puppet regime. Mason relaunched Siege, in which he preached violence, racial strife, and an all-out war against the hated "System."

01:01:01.327 --> 01:01:23.172
In his search for extremist mentors, Mason became obsessed with Charles Manson (born 1934). Manson was a notorious killer serving life imprisonment for conspiracy in the murders of actress Sharon Tate and others in 1969. Although Manson had carved a swastika into his own forehead, his politics were vague.

01:01:23.172 --> 01:01:55.087
However, Mason regarded Manson as the supreme outlaw. He adopted the convicted criminal as the spiritual leader of his new Nazi group, the Universal Order. The name came from Manson. Mason's Nazi religion embraced both Hitler and Manson as saviors. This combined Koehl's messianic piety with the millenarian violence of Tomassi. In the pages of Siege, Mason paid extravagant tribute to Hitler, Tommasi, Manson, and Savitri Devi.

01:01:55.087 --> 01:02:11.215
By the mid-1960s, WUNS had already acted as a pilot scheme for exporting American neo-Nazism to Europe. This Euro-American partnership was followed by another Rockwell heir, the National Socialist Party of America (NSPA).

01:02:11.215 --> 01:02:43.727
Frank Collin founded the NSPA in 1970. Collin was a partly Jewish fascist. He was expelled from the NSWPP due to internal party friction and slurs about his racial ancestry. In the late 1970s, the NSPA gained massive publicity. They held violent rallies in the Jewish district of Skokie near Chicago. The NSPA has often been involved in violent incidents with Klansmen. They also attempted an abortive invasion of the Caribbean island of Dominica.

01:02:43.727 --> 01:03:19.737
In November 1979, members of a local branch were implicated in the killing of five left-wing radicals. These radicals were attending an anti-Klu Klux Klan rally in Greensboro, North Carolina. The NSPA became important in the international neo-Nazi scene as the sponsor and supporter of the offshore German NSDAP Auslands- und Aufbauorganisation (NSDAP-AO). Gerhard (Gary) Lauck, a German American neo-Nazi, founded this group in West Germany in 1973.

01:03:19.737 --> 01:03:27.759
After Bonn authorities expelled Lauck in 1974, the group moved its operations to the United States.

01:03:27.759 --> 01:04:00.271
Lauck initially based himself at the Arlington, Virginia, headquarters of the WUNS. This organization aligned with Matt Koehl's NSWPP. Several U.S. Nazi groups provided financial backing. Later, the NSDAP-AO joined forces with the NSPA. They now share offices in Lincoln, Nebraska. The group originally formed in exile from Germany to campaign for the legalization of a National Socialist party there. Over the past twenty years, the NSDAP-AO's scope has expanded dramatically to span the globe.

01:04:00.271 --> 01:04:30.649
The NSPA and NSDAP-AO publish a joint monthly periodical called New Order. It appears in English, German, Swedish, Hungarian, French, Dutch, Spanish, Italian, Portuguese, and Danish. The U.S. Commission on Civil Rights described the NSDAP-AO as "one of the world's most influential neo-Nazi propaganda outfits … the biggest supplier of propaganda to neo-Nazis."

01:04:30.649 --> 01:04:41.657
Lauck's organization still aims to provide support and publications to neo-Nazis in Germany without hindrance, even though they operate under constitutional restrictions.

01:04:41.657 --> 01:05:16.559
To achieve this, the NSDAP-AO publishes a German-language journal, NS Kampfruf,. It also makes thousands of leaflets and labels with Nazi slogans for illegal distribution in Germany. The group claims to have many secret members in Germany. During the 1980s, it expanded its activities to Scandinavia and Austria. In May 1995, Gary Lauck was arrested in Denmark. He was later convicted in Germany for distributing illegal neo-Nazi literature. He received a prison sentence.

01:05:16.559 --> 01:05:52.057
However, his removal barely stopped his organization's propaganda. The group has effectively absorbed the NSPA. A similar outfit called Liberty Bell Publications is run by George P. Dietz in Reedy, West Virginia. Dietz is a farm broker and a former member of the Hitler Youth. He moved to the United States in 1957. Besides selling many anti-Semitic books, Nazi literature, regalia, and replica party badges made in Taiwan, Liberty Bell publishes its own periodical, Liberty Bell,.

01:05:52.057 --> 01:06:06.820
It also publishes a neo-Nazi bulletin, DerSchulungsbrief,, for distribution in Germany. After Rockwell died, the National Alliance became the other major successor to the NSWPP.

01:06:06.820 --> 01:06:37.199
William Pierce led it. He had previously edited National Socialist World. Thirty years later, Pierce remains the most important neo-Nazi organizer and publisher in the United States. He wrote The Turner Diaries, a cult novel about race war. He also made regular radio broadcasts. He met with top nationalist leaders of European parties. He involved himself with youth culture and white power music through Resistance Records.

01:06:37.199 --> 01:06:45.391
These actions have fully justified his status as the key intellectual of the original American Nazi Party leadership.

01:06:45.391 --> 01:07:20.292
The National Alliance traces its roots to the National Youth Alliance. Willis Carto of the Liberty Lobby founded it in late 1968. It grew out of a campaign organization called Youth for Wallace. That group was originally linked to Governor George Wallace. The NYA aimed to fight anarchist and left-wing groups on university campuses. It also sought to make students more open to right-wing ideas. It stood for law and order. It opposed black power, hippies, and the drug culture.

01:07:20.292 --> 01:07:56.388
The NYA's racist and anti-Semitic policies quickly drew the attention of Pierce and other NSWPP activists. Internal strife split the organization into two factions by the spring of 1971. One faction, now known as Youth Action, stayed loyal to Carto. The other faction, led by Pierce, became known as the National Alliance by 1974. Pierce quickly built the organization into a new Nazi lobby group. He used National Vanguard (formerly Attack!), for this.

01:07:56.388 --> 01:08:26.169
It was published as a tabloid from 1970 to 1982. It then continued in magazine form. True to the tone of his racist editorials in the WUNS periodical, Pierce promoted the belief in a Jewish conspiracy. He claimed this conspiracy aimed to destroy the white race through socialism, black power, the banking system, and racial mixing. Pierce set up his headquarters in Washington, D.C. He built wide connections with the American far right.

01:08:26.169 --> 01:09:00.473
National Vanguard spread widely among neo-Nazi groups. The National Alliance worked with several foreign organizations. John Tyndall, then leader of Britain's National Front, visited Pierce in 1979. The Alliance also contacted other British groups. These included the National Party, a short-lived successor to the NF, and the League of St. George. Pierce stayed in regular contact with Tyndall. He attended the British National Party's annual rally in November 1995.

01:09:00.473 --> 01:09:12.079
In the early 1980s, Pierce avoided Washington's growing black population. He bought a 400-acre retreat near Hillsboro, a remote village in West Virginia's Appalachian Mountains.

01:09:12.079 --> 01:09:45.529
The property sits behind a high barbed-wire fence. There, he runs a large bookselling service focused on Western culture and pagan tradition. It sells many Penguin Classics. He also edits National Vanguard with his staff. He preaches a racist message in his "Cosmotheist Church" inside the compound. The compound displays a Nordic man-rune that represents creation. This part of his group shows the pan-Aryan religious nature of his mission.

01:09:45.529 --> 01:10:19.748
In his newsletter, Pierce quotes Savitri Devi on the ultimate purpose of evolution. She calls it "that mysterious and unfailing wisdom according to which nature lives and creates: the impersonal wisdom of the primeval forest and of the ocean depth and of the spheres in the dark fields of space." Pierce's Cosmotheism assigns each race and species a specific role in relation to the Whole. He says the Negro is content to idle. He says the Jew acts as a ferment of decay.

01:10:19.748 --> 01:10:53.967
He says the white man is guided by the Divine Spark within him. This spark leads him ever upward toward the Creator, who is a living part of his Being. This call to unending evolutionary progress uses a Platonic doctrine of souls. It limits the ascent to the Godhead to Aryan individuals. Here, Cosmotheism reflects Lanz von Liebenfels's prewar Ariosophy. Pierce's racist imagination is driven by a zeal to save the Aryan race.

01:10:53.967 --> 01:11:24.687
He wants to build a territory of white rule in the Appalachian Mountains. This idea matches beliefs in the Christian Identity movement. That movement got its original inspiration from late-nineteenth-century British-Israelism. This loose Christian group in England claimed that Anglo-Saxon races were the lost tribes of Israel. They saw themselves as distinct from the Jews of Judah. But they showed little or no hostility toward Jews.

01:11:24.687 --> 01:11:32.537
By the 1930s, American followers of British-Israelism embraced a fierce anti-Semitic theology.

01:11:32.537 --> 01:11:52.164
They viewed Jews as the unyielding enemies of the Aryan race in America. Since the 1970s, the Christian Identity movement has been a loose network. It includes the Church of Jesus Christ Christian, Aryan Nations; the Church of Christ; and the New Christian Crusade Church.

01:11:52.164 --> 01:12:08.207
James Warner, formerly with the NSWPP, led the New Christian Crusade Church. It is now superseded by the Christian Defense League. Aryan Nations advocates creating a territorial sanctuary.

01:12:08.207 --> 01:12:31.673
It eventually aims for a white sovereign national state in the Pacific Northwest states. Religious feelings of election, demonology, and an inevitable apocalyptic battle color Identity thinking. This battle is between the Aryans and the Zionist-led forces of darkness. Pierce was not a supporter of Identity.

01:12:31.673 --> 01:12:51.897
Yet his own form of Nazi racism shows a similar focus on the threatened white Aryan elect and a coming Armageddon against the Jewish political establishment. Pierce's underground right-wing novel, The Turner Diaries (1978), presents an eyewitness account of a future armed struggle.

01:12:51.897 --> 01:13:24.409
White revolutionaries fight the "System." They see this System as an oppressive and corrupt U.S. government. It is dominated by liberals, Jews, blacks, and other minorities. All these groups are committed to anti-racist, egalitarian public policy. The novel offers a compelling narrative. It describes the activities of a young white patriot, Earl Turner, and his fellow fighters in the "Organization." This happens after a government crackdown on private firearm possession.

01:13:24.409 --> 01:13:53.849
They become more politicized as the government takes ever more forceful measures to achieve complete racial integration. Hated racial-equality police pursue them. Turner and his confederates start to fight back. They launch a campaign of sabotage and assassination. As the struggle escalates, an all-out race war breaks out across the United States. The Organization uses guerrilla tactics against the System.

01:13:53.849 --> 01:14:29.775
This leads to civil war after a successful military attack on Los Angeles. Local armed forces stage a racial mutiny. Many soldiers defect to the rebels. The Organization enforces strict racial segregation. It also forces the collection and expulsion of the colored population. These actions create a large white enclave in southern California. This enclave serves as a base for attacking the rest of the country. Pierce's novel celebrates detailed descriptions of mayhem and total destruction.

01:14:29.775 --> 01:15:02.799
The Organization gathers new forces daily. It strikes at other major U.S. cities. This is a war of attrition against the Jewish-dominated multiracial establishment still based in Washington and New York. Nuclear bombs destroy Miami, Charleston, Detroit, and New York. The Organization attacks Israel and the Soviet Union. More than 60 million people die in the United States alone. Total savagery and a return to barbarism mark a period of five "dark years."

01:15:02.799 --> 01:15:23.364
This ends with the final "liberation" of North America in early 1999. The Turner Diaries describe a white revolution against the claimed political control of the U.S.A. by Jews. They also describe the ethnic cleansing of blacks, Hispanics, and other non-white people in America.

01:15:23.364 --> 01:15:53.231
Pierce's Nazi inspiration is clear in many references and passages. These parts strongly recall the Nazi extermination of Jews during the Second World War. The Organization issues proclamations. They warn of severe consequences for anyone who knowingly hides a Jew or other non-white person during the deportations. The blacks are quickly expelled to territory held by the System. The Jews and other mixed-race people are marched to their death in a canyon.

01:15:53.231 --> 01:16:21.647
This scene reminds one of the 1941 massacre of Ukrainian Jews in the ravine of Babi Yar near Kiev. To instill terror and correct racial thinking in the civilian population of the California enclave, about 60,000 anti-racists are hanged in a single day of lynchings. These victims include former leading politicians, lawyers, media and press personnel, teachers, and priests.

01:16:21.647 --> 01:16:56.036
The victims bear placards that read "I betrayed my race." Female partners in mixed couples are killed in the same way. Their caption reads, "I defiled my race." The small beginnings and growth of the Organization reflect the rise of the Nazi Party in Weimar Germany. Its inner elite is called the Order. This group is identified as a successor to the SS. The Aryan revolution is seen as a replay of the uncompleted Holocaust in the 1940s.

01:16:56.036 --> 01:17:28.889
"The dream of a White world" is finally realized "just 110 years after the birth of the Great One [i.e., Adolf Hitler]." The white revolution is ultimately global. After a nuclear attack, the Arabs overrun Israel. Anti-Semitism becomes common in European states and the Soviet Union. The white Aryan forces in America soon win in Europe. The takeover happened in a massive, Europe-wide rush during the summer and fall of 1999.

01:17:28.889 --> 01:18:01.743
A cleansing hurricane of change swept over the continent. It cleared away the refuse of over a millennium of alien ideology. It also removed a century or more of deep moral and material decay. For a moment, blood flowed ankle-deep in the streets of many of Europe's great cities. The race traitors met a common fate. So did the offspring of generations of dysgenic breeding. So did hordes of Gastarbeiter. The great dawn of the New Era broke over the Western world.

01:18:01.743 --> 01:18:36.388
The Organization achieves global victory by destroying the Chinese. It uses chemical, biological, and radiological weapons in this campaign. It then creates a "Great Eastern Waste" zone. This zone covers 16 million square miles. It stretches from the Urals to the Pacific and from the Arctic to the Indian Ocean. Pierce's projection of anti-Semitic and racist Nazi fantasies into a millenarian vision of universal Nazi rule is unique.

01:18:36.388 --> 01:19:10.777
His paranoid view of liberal, democratic society carries strong religious overtones in its fervor and apocalyptic release. A foreword, supposedly written a century later, describes Earl Turner as being born in 43 BNE (Before New Era) in Los Angeles. This former metropolitan area is now occupied by the Aryan communities of Eckartsville and Wesselton. These towns are named for Hitler's mentor Dietrich Eckart and Nazi martyr Horst Wessel.

01:19:10.777 --> 01:19:42.948
Writing of the early beginnings of the white revolution in California, Turner prophesies, "we are forging the nucleus of a new society, a whole new civilization, which will rise from the ashes of the old. … There is no way a society based on Aryan values and an Aryan outlook can evolve from a society which has succumbed to Jewish spiritual corruption." The prophetic and religious feel of universal Nazism has given The Turner Diaries an international underground readership.

01:19:42.948 --> 01:20:12.559
American and European neo-Nazi groups circulate the book widely as a modern Mein Kampf. In the 1980s, the National Front sold the novel. It has also strongly influenced the recent growth of neo-Nazi terrorism in Britain (see chapter 2). Pierce's predicted end of the world soon appeared in the United States. In September 1983, a militant racist sect called The Order formed in Metaline Falls, Washington.

01:20:12.559 --> 01:20:19.471
People also called this terrorist group the Brüders Schweigen, or Silent Brotherhood.

01:20:19.471 --> 01:20:46.948
Robert Jay Mathews, born in 1953, founded the group. He had a long history of ties to the far right. Mathews planned to create a small cell. This cell would have the will and resources to attack and overthrow the "Zionist Occupation Government" (ZOG) of the United States. He needed money to buy weapons for a guerrilla campaign against the state. He expected this campaign to lead to a mass revolt by the white population.

01:20:46.948 --> 01:21:19.119
The Order started its operations with large-scale counterfeiting and armed robbery. In July 1984, they stole $3.8 million from a Brinks armored car in Ukiah, California. They committed other acts of violence. They assassinated Alan Berg, a Jewish radio presenter in Denver. Berg was known for his open opposition to right-wing groups. In December 1984, the FBI killed Mathews during a siege on Whidbey Island, Washington.

01:21:19.119 --> 01:21:34.905
The remaining Order members were captured in 1985 and 1986. The inspiration for The Order came directly from The Turner Diaries. Mathews told recruits that his organization was based on the fictional inner elite.

01:21:34.905 --> 01:22:09.721
He presented the book to members. The novel shares many other parallels with the group. These include the use of code names. They also produced "hit lists" of racial and ideological enemies. The group executed traitors. Members took an oath in a ritual. They swore upon "the green graves of our sires [and] the children in the wombs of our wives." They swore "to do whatever is necessary to deliver our people from the Jew and bring total victory to the Aryan race."

01:22:09.721 --> 01:22:40.441
Mathews's own religious inclination was pagan Odinist. He also had Christian Identity connections with Aryan Nations. A quarter of The Order's recruits had Identity associations with Aryan Nations and the Church of Jesus Christ Christian. David Lane drove the getaway car after the Berg murder. He was an Identity church member. He also founded the 14 Word Press. Its motto has become a mantra for white identity groups across the world.

01:22:40.441 --> 01:23:01.092
The motto is "We must secure the existence of our people and a future for white children." The Turner Diaries has in turn influenced the Christian Identity movement. In the latter half of the 1980s, Christian Identity groups developed varied plans for the secession of a separate Aryan territory.

01:23:01.092 --> 01:23:27.801
This theme was anticipated by Pierce's novel. The plan included establishing a white California as the first stage of the revolution. Pierce popularized the idea that the U.S. government is a Jewish-controlled puppet regime. This idea has now become a staple of far-right racist discourse under the ZOG acronym. The book's power to motivate far-right terrorism remains undiminished.

01:23:27.801 --> 01:23:37.529
Friends recall that Timothy McVeigh, who was convicted of the Oklahoma City bombing of April 1995, repeatedly reread the novel.

01:23:37.529 --> 01:23:54.852
The Oklahoma City bombing was the largest terrorist atrocity in the history of the United States. It is claimed that McVeigh also copied the bomb attack on an FBI office described in the book's pages. He copied it down to the smallest details of his delivery and timing.

01:23:54.852 --> 01:24:27.791
The quick defeat of The Order pushed the radical right to plan more secretive and desperate strategies for a race war. Many Nazis now reject all organizational structures as too easy for officials to infiltrate. Instead, they support terrorist acts by individuals or very small, independent cells. Bombs and murder replace nuclear weapons and open war. William Pierce again provided fictional inspiration with his second novel, Hunter (1989).

01:24:27.791 --> 01:24:36.751
It describes Oscar Yeagar's one-man war against Jews and colored people, especially mixed-race couples.

01:24:36.751 --> 01:25:14.297
The idea of the "lone wolf" was not new. Misfits and psychopaths in the American Nazi movement, such as Joseph G. Christopher, Joseph Paul Franklin (also known as James Vaughn), and Frank G. Spisak, committed serial racial killings in the early 1980s. John Hinckley, the would-be assassin of President Ronald Reagan, also had Nazi ties. While James Mason praised these murders in the pages of Siege, Pierce was outlining a new tactic to counter the state's superior military power.

01:25:14.297 --> 01:25:42.116
Hunter suggests that isolated, small-scale, and untraceable acts of violence can raise public racial awareness. They can also effectively demoralize and destabilize multiracial society. Richard Kelly Hoskins, a follower of Christian Identity, contributed another strand to this thinking. He wrote about "the Phineas Priesthood" using biblical references in Numbers and Psalms.

01:25:42.116 --> 01:26:17.444
In the story, the Lord gets angry because the Israelites live with Moabite women. Phinehas, Aaron's grandson, kills a mixed-race couple with his spear. The Lord is pleased. He spares the Israelites from the plague. He makes a covenant of "an everlasting priesthood" with the zealous Phinehas (Numbers 25:6-13). The psalm text repeats the story. It says Phinehas "executed judgment" and the plague stopped (Psalms 106:30).

01:26:17.444 --> 01:26:24.868
Hoskins claims that corruption and disease always happen when strangers force their way into Christian society.

01:26:24.868 --> 01:26:55.844
He identifies a line of "Phineas Priests" who have purged aliens through history. This line ranges from King Arthur and Robin Hood to the Ku Klux Klan and the SS. The modern Phineas Priesthood is a cult of lone killers. They never link up. They carry out independent acts of murder against blacks, Jews, homosexuals, liberals, and left-wingers. They see all these groups as enemies of the white race.

01:26:55.844 --> 01:27:14.532
Louis Beam, another Identity figure with a Texas Klan background, provided a strategic framework for these acts of individual terrorism. Beam had been involved in The Order and was a leading defendant in the 1988 Fort Worth sedition trial that arose from its activities.

01:27:14.532 --> 01:27:47.727
The FBI shooting of the Weaver family at their home in Ruby Ridge, Idaho, led to a key conference of patriots, far-right groups, and Christian Identity followers in Estes Park, Colorado, in October 1992. There, Beam outlined a new plan for militant opposition to ZOG in his highly influential essay, "Leaderless Resistance." He believed that anti-government resistance using hierarchical command structures was hopeless and suicidal.

01:27:47.727 --> 01:28:18.959
The cellular model developed by Russian revolutionary communism had an advantage, because losing a single cell left the rest of the structure intact. However, such cells required central direction and outside resources that the far right could not afford. Beam concluded that the only rational strategy was "leaderless resistance" or "phantom cells." Single individuals or tiny groups should operate in total isolation from one another.

01:28:18.959 --> 01:28:48.399
Their common outlook and similar reactions to given situations would remove the need for central direction. He acknowledged that alternative communications media could reinforce these uniform attitudes, an evident reference to the growing use of the Internet by far-right and racist groups worldwide. Beam, a Vietnam War veteran with a gift for passionate speaking, was a key ideological inspiration for the far-right underground in the 1990s.

01:28:48.399 --> 01:28:54.713
Leaderless resistance appealed to Nazis who had given up on mass elections or armed uprisings.

01:28:54.713 --> 01:29:23.812
It promised safety from enemy spies. It avoided the awkward question of why the Nazi movement could not attract a large following. It suggested that stealth could succeed where heroism had failed. Beam's message was clear, even though he never mentioned specific violent acts. With its random acts of mayhem, sabotage, and murder, leaderless resistance would be an "intelligence nightmare" for the government.

01:29:23.812 --> 01:30:00.505
Individuals linked to The Order in the United States, Combat 18 in Britain, and White Aryan Resistance (Vit Arikst Motstånd, VAM) in Sweden have now adopted this strategy. Acting alone or in small groups, Nazis pick a target, then strike and destroy it. The lack of formal organization makes official responses hesitant and detection difficult. Timothy McVeigh's move from the Michigan militia to his "lone wolf" bombing in Oklahoma City suggests a similar tactical progression.

01:30:00.505 --> 01:30:34.553
Harold Covington briefly led the American Nazi scene. After his role in the NSPA at the Greensboro massacre, he left the United States. He traveled to Ireland, Britain, and Rhodesia. There, he married an Irish woman and gained dual citizenship. Back in the U.S., he replaced Frank Collin as NSPA leader in 1980. He then won 56,000 votes in a primary election. He ran as the Republican candidate for state attorney general. In 1981, he founded his own Excalibur Society.

01:30:34.553 --> 01:31:07.492
This group pushed Nazi policies on racial, social, and economic issues. He stayed close to Sean McGuire, a Klansman with strong IRA sympathies. At the same time, Covington wrote his own "Mein Kampf." His book The March up Country outlines the Nazi path to power in America. Later, in the summer of 1991, Covington started planning an international network of Nazi terrorist cells in Europe. These cells shared common enemies and used modern computer communications to link up.

01:31:07.492 --> 01:31:37.700
He contacted the Swedish VAM. This group's guerrilla activities reached Norway and eastern Germany. In 1991-92, he worked closely with the Sargent brothers to set up Combat 18 in Britain. This Nazi militia sends out secret bulletins. These bulletins list the private addresses of enemies linked to left-wing, green, and peace politics. Individual cell members then issue death threats and attack these targets.

01:31:37.700 --> 01:32:06.799
Covington re-established the NSWPP in April 1994 from his base in Chapel Hill, North Carolina. For a short time, the NSWPP was again the most active self-proclaimed Nazi party in the United States. Using the Orwellian pseudonym Winston Smith, Covington produced a huge amount of propaganda. This included a daily Internet bulletin and a weekly paper, Resistance, in loose-leaf format.

01:32:06.799 --> 01:32:40.335
He kept strong domestic and international connections through e-mail and a website. Staying true to Rockwell's original vision, the new NSWPP was a revolutionary Aryan party. It aimed to ensure the survival of white people in North America by creating a sovereign Aryan Republic. Covington's program was aggressive and inflammatory. It sought to mobilize unhappy white voters against an administration that grants voting rights to racial outsiders to guarantee its own political survival.

01:32:40.335 --> 01:33:00.388
Covington had issued dire warnings about President Bill Clinton's second term. He foresaw a "terrible time of tyranny, corruption, and collapse into Brazil-style squalor." However, his book and terrorist links show that Covington actually despaired of mass electoral strategy.

01:33:00.388 --> 01:33:21.124
Given worsening racial conditions in America, such as racial quotas, hate crime laws, and media vilification of white identity, he believes it is time for the Nazi movement to accept armed struggle as the next phase of its development. He is no longer fronting the revived NSWPP.

01:33:21.124 --> 01:33:51.929
Compared to native right-wing radical groups like the Klu Klux Klan, the Christian Identity movement, Posse Comitatus, and survivalists, American Nazi groups such as the NSWPP, the New Order, and the National Alliance seem exotic and distinctly un-American. American neo-Nazism has tried to attach its own religious doctrine to complex issues of black desegregation and mass Third World immigration.

01:33:51.929 --> 01:34:25.465
This doctrine is rooted in a dualist anti-Semitic demonology. These issues continue to cause genuine social stress. However, most anti-integration groups, such as the White Citizens Councils, were very pro-American. They were by no means anti-Semitic. They resisted any Nazi association. This critical gap between the political circumstances of integration and anti-Semitic ideology helps explain why American neo-Nazism remains a sectarian phenomenon.

01:34:25.465 --> 01:34:57.807
For any neo-Nazi movement to succeed beyond its sectarian activities, it must build a wider base among alienated sections of white American society. There is some evidence that efforts have been made to carry the message to groups such as skinheads (see chapter 10), the Patriots (see chapter 14), and white prisoners, especially in the South. Yet in some ways, neo-Nazism fits into a tradition of religious fundamentalism in the United States.

01:34:57.807 --> 01:35:25.284
After Rockwell's showy gospel, Matt Koehl led a Nazi church. In their isolated community, American neo-Nazis follow a prophetic religion. They view Hitler as a Christ figure and Rockwell as St. Paul. As Jim Saleam has argued, neo-Nazis see. Nazi Germany's twelve years under Hitler's ministry were times of revealed faith and miracles.

01:35:25.284 --> 01:35:57.113
The war was the crucifixion. The swastika served as the cross, a talisman against evil. The Nazi leaders were Hitler's disciples. The Nuremberg trials created martyrs and drove the faith into the political catacombs. No one spoke Hitler's name for fear of the Jews. However, Rockwell converted to this new faith and took on the mission of spreading its doctrine. While Hitler preached only to Germans, Rockwell would convert all nations.

01:35:57.113 --> 01:36:23.311
Saleam compares Rockwell's assassination to a disciple's betrayal, like Judas's. He says Matt Koehl becomes the first pope of a church built on orthodoxy. Koehl receives the keys of salvation and the power to excommunicate from the one true party. There is a structural, if not theological, parallel between the Christian gospel and the racial evangel of neo-Nazism.

01:36:23.311 --> 01:36:51.556
This prophetic and structural similarity makes the doctrine of racial salvation understandable to people in a culture where Christian fundamentalism has always flourished. This is especially true given the millenarianism and the messianic status of Hitler in neo-Nazism. George Lincoln Rockwell's Nazi roots go back to the patriotic, pro-German, and appeasement groups of the 1930s.

01:36:51.556 --> 01:37:10.927
Rockwell and his successors in America have kept selling a similar mix of anti-Semitism and ultranationalism, adding new postwar worries. Cold War anti-communism has now given way to a suspicion of federal power and a "New World Order."

01:37:10.927 --> 01:37:40.367
Yet the constant issue is white identity. This involves racial hatred aimed at blacks and other non-white groups to counter the effects of the civil rights movement and equal-opportunity laws from the early 1960s to today. Second, because the Third Reich was defeated, neo-Nazis push a stronger form of anti-Semitism. They promise to finish the Holocaust in a new war against American and international Jews.

01:37:40.367 --> 01:38:10.745
Third, and perhaps the defining feature of Nazi sects, they worship Adolf Hitler as the savior of a white, Western world. In all Nazi groups, Hitler's birthday is regularly celebrated as the high point of their year. This is when they collect and display Nazi relics in secret shrines. Both the symbols and the myths of American Nazism reflect the behavior of a persecuted religious sect that prepares for violent action against a fallen world.

01:38:10.745 --> 01:38:10.845


01:38:10.845 --> 01:38:18.355
2. The British Nazi Underground. The Axis powers were completely defeated in 1945.

01:38:18.355 --> 01:38:47.795
The Nazi atrocities in the concentration camps were confirmed. This did not stop a fascist tradition from reappearing in Europe for long. In March 1950, various European neo-fascist and neo-Nazi movements held their first postwar gathering in Rome. In May 1951, about a hundred delegates from parties in Germany, Italy, Austria, France, Spain, and Sweden met in Malmö, in southern Sweden.

01:38:47.795 --> 01:39:19.965
Within a decade, the larger neo-fascist parties in Europe moved toward forming a new International. In March 1962, they founded the National European Party. This happened at a convention in Venice. The convention included Sir Oswald Mosley's Union Movement, the Deutsche Reichspartei, Jeune Europe, and the Movimento Sociale Italiano. Postwar fascist Internationals usually tried to distance themselves from their wartime past.

01:39:19.965 --> 01:39:47.784
They avoided embarrassing mentions of Hitler, the SS, Nazism, and the Holocaust. Mosley updated the politics of his prewar British Union of Fascists. He appealed for European unity, a key part of the Union Movement's 1948 national election campaign. Mosley held strong loyalty on the British far right. However, his strategy drew challenges from nationalists and unreconstructed fascists.

01:39:47.784 --> 01:39:57.597
In spring 1962, Colin Jordan, a British neo-Nazi leader who admired Hitler, dropped this caution for the first time since the war.

01:39:57.597 --> 01:40:37.192
Jordan revived Nazi symbols like brown shirts, breeches, jackboots, and swastika armbands. He also used slogans such as "Sieg Heil," "Juden 'raus," and the Horst Wessel Song. In August 1962, Jordan and others founded the World Union of National Socialists (WUNS). This group included George Lincoln Rockwell, Savitri Devi, Bruno Lüdtke, and representatives from Nazi groups in seven countries. They presented WUNS as a self-proclaimed Nazi International.

01:40:37.192 --> 01:40:58.269
Colin Jordan's British neo-Nazism was a radical reaction to the presence of a colored population. American Nazis protested the emancipation of a Negro underclass in the United States. The British protest targeted the rapid growth of colored immigration from New Commonwealth countries starting in the late 1950s.

01:40:58.269 --> 01:41:32.403
Beyond this reactive racial nationalism, Jordan was mainly inspired by a prewar fascist tradition of anti-Semitism. He also held an unalloyed admiration for Hitler and German National Socialism. These ideals have remained the hallmarks of Colin Jordan's political program from the war years into the 1990s. This makes him the leading representative of the postwar Hitler cult in Britain. Looking at Colin Jordan's career offers important lessons about today's militant Nazi underground.

01:41:32.403 --> 01:42:01.672
Contemporary terrorist groups like Combat 18 and David Myatt's National-Socialist Movement trace their lineage back to Jordan. Many violent groups in America revere George Lincoln Rockwell in the same way. Colin Jordan's rise to prominence occurred against the background of mass immigration. Therefore, the British story holds wider significance for developments in Europe today. John Colin Campbell Jordan was born in Birmingham, England, in 1923.

01:42:01.672 --> 01:42:31.368
He went to Warwick School, a top preparatory school. There, he won a scholarship to study history at Cambridge University. He paused his studies to volunteer for the Fleet Air Arm. However, he failed his naval pilot's course. He did not give up. Instead, he joined the Royal Air Force and waited for new flying training. He says that by the end of 1944, his political views were fully formed. He declared that he opposed continuing the war.

01:42:31.368 --> 01:43:01.149
He also supported negotiating a peace with Germany. As part of the deferred service personnel, he was then sent to the Royal Army Medical Corps. There, he became an educational instructor. After leaving the military, he returned to Sidney Sussex College, Cambridge, in 1946 to finish his degree. Like other older student veterans, Jordan was very active in university life. He worked on the staff of the university newspaper, Varsity.

01:43:01.149 --> 01:43:24.104
He also spoke from the front bench in debates at the Union. He received a second-class degree in 1949. While at university, Jordan contacted British nationalist and neo-fascist groups to promote their cause at Cambridge. He joined the anti-Semitic British People's Party (BPP) and was elected to its national council.

01:43:24.104 --> 01:43:53.459
John Beckett founded this party in the summer of 1939. Beckett had previously led the National Socialist League in 1937-38 with William Joyce. Joyce later became known as Lord Haw-Haw for his pro-Nazi broadcasts from Berlin during the war. He was executed as a traitor. The BPP committed to social credit economics. It aimed to counter what it saw as the dangers of usury and sought peace with Germany.

01:43:53.459 --> 01:44:21.875
Under the patronage of the Duke of Bedford, the BPP survived the war and the internment of British fascists. Jordan also organized the University Nationalist Club. After leaving Cambridge, he founded the Birmingham Nationalist Club. He ran this club until moving to Leeds for a teaching post. At this time, he became a strong opponent of communism. He published his first book, Fraudulent Conversion (1955).

01:44:21.875 --> 01:44:49.011
The book asserted that Jews ran the Soviet Union, despite the apparent anti-Semitism and pro-Arab line of late Stalinism. Jordan argued that the struggle between communism and Zionism was an internal Jewish feud over the best way to achieve world domination. Arnold Spencer Leese (1878-1956) was Jordan's most important contact at Cambridge and later.

01:44:49.011 --> 01:45:22.291
Leese was a committed anti-Semite. In 1929, he founded the Imperial Fascist League. This small party had two hundred members. During the 1930s, it was the most pro-German and openly anti-Semitic group in England. The League always stayed independent of Oswald Mosley's British Union of Fascists. Leese saw Mosley as an opportunist. He argued that Mosley's fascism did not rest on racial nationalism. Leese suspected that Mosley's first wife had Jewish ancestry.

01:45:22.291 --> 01:45:52.157
He called Mosley a "kosher fascist." He claimed Mosley was a Jewish agent planted to discredit fascism in Britain. Leese published a pro-Nazi magazine, The Fascist, from 1929 to 1939. During the war, authorities detained him under the 18B regulation against suspected German "fifth columnists." After his release, he resumed anti-Semitic publishing in Guildford.

01:45:52.157 --> 01:46:24.157
He did this with his abusive periodical, Gothic Ripples, which ran from 1945 to 1956. In his first postwar book, The Jewish War of Survival (1945), Leese admitted that the Jews had won a victory when Hitler was defeated. However, he argued that a strong policy of anti-Semitism could still break their power. In 1947, he was briefly imprisoned again for helping two fugitive Dutch members of the Waffen-SS.

01:46:24.157 --> 01:46:55.475
Leese's views became even cruder after the war. He believed that Jews were encouraging immigration from non-white countries to dilute Britain's racial stock. This would allow the Aryan civilization to be destroyed. Leese credited the Aryans with creating all of civilization. Yet he saw Negroes as the most inferior type of human being. Like Hitler, Leese regarded the Jews as an anti-race, an infernal opponent of Aryan mankind.

01:46:55.475 --> 01:47:03.496
Leese was encouraged by the interest of Jordan, in whom he saw a youthful, intelligent, and enthusiastic successor.

01:47:03.496 --> 01:47:36.179
For his part, Jordan regarded Leese as a major mentor figure. The two men remained close friends until Leese's death. Leese's widow, who taught her cat to give the Hitler salute, was a staunch supporter of Jordan in his subsequent struggles on the far-right scene. Leese's influence on Jordan was a crucial factor in Jordan's combination of racial populism in reaction to colored immigration and a prewar tradition of anti-Semitism. Jordan returned to the Midlands to teach in Coventry.

01:47:36.179 --> 01:48:12.531
He joined the League of Empire Loyalists (LEL). This lobby group was founded in 1954 by A. K. Chesterton (1899-1973). Chesterton had been a deputy to Mosley in the prewar British Union of Fascists. The LEL aimed to reverse the decolonization policies pursued by the Conservative government. Like Rockwell, who initially sought a home in more conventional far-right groups, Jordan was drawn to the LEL. He liked its aggressive defense of white rule in Britain's African colonies.

01:48:12.531 --> 01:48:42.824
With noisy rallies and outrageous publicity stunts, the LEL served as a vehicle for vigorous nationalist protest. Jordan became the Midlands organizer for the LEL. However, he found little room there for the anti-Semitic and Nazi ideas he shared with Arnold Leese. It was not until the late 1950s that he found a domestic issue with potential for a mass movement on the extreme right. This issue was opposition to colored immigration to Britain.

01:48:42.824 --> 01:48:47.517
After World War II, Western European economies lacked enough workers.

01:48:47.517 --> 01:49:12.520
They solved this by bringing in workers from other countries. In Britain, these workers usually came from its colonies or former colonies, especially the West Indies, India, and Pakistan. The first group from the West Indies arrived in 1948. From 1948 to 1954, between 8,000 and 10,000 immigrants came to Britain each year.

01:49:12.520 --> 01:49:20.712
In 1954 and 1955, immigration from the West Indies rose to over 20,000 per year.

01:49:20.712 --> 01:49:52.797
Immigration from India and Pakistan rose to about 10,000. Between 1955 and 1957, a total of 132,000 colored immigrants from the Commonwealth arrived in Britain. Of these, 80,000 had come from the West Indies. People viewed the newcomers with some worry. This was especially true in the working-class communities where the newcomers expected to settle. However, all major political parties wanted to avoid making immigration a political issue.

01:49:52.797 --> 01:50:18.056
It was therefore foreseeable that new political groups would arise to demand immigration control. The National Labour Party (NLP) and the White Defence League (WDL) handled the immigration issue in an inflammatory way. John Edward Bean (born 1927) and Colin Jordan founded these groups in 1957 after leaving the LEL.

01:50:18.056 --> 01:50:45.789
In August 1958, race riots broke out in Nottingham. Similar riots followed in Notting Hill in West London in September. Jordan ran the White Defence League from Arnold Leese House at 74 Princedale Road in Notting Hill. Leese's widow had placed the house at his disposal. He organized nightly rallies in the streets of this immigrant neighborhood throughout the tense, hot summer of 1958.

01:50:45.789 --> 01:51:08.061
He also published a local newspaper, Black and White News, and a flood of racist pamphlets. These publications provoked strong feelings of resentment against the newcomers. Colored immigration gave new life to old racist and Nazi ideas. Jordan believed the immigration issue was crucial because it made people think about race.

01:51:08.061 --> 01:51:43.731
This made them more open to his main anti-Semitic beliefs. In 1959, he promoted Nordic racial unity by publishing a small periodical called The Nationalist. By February 1960, the WDL and NLP had merged to form the new British National Party (BNP). Its motto was "For Race and Nation." Andrew Fountaine, a Norfolk landowner, became president. Mrs. Leese became vice-president. Jordan became national organizer.

01:51:43.731 --> 01:52:01.565
John Tyndall, who had also been in the LEL, became a founder member. The extreme right in Britain looked very strong between 1960 and 1962. In 1960, about 60,000 immigrants from the West Indies, India, and Pakistan joined the population.

01:52:01.565 --> 01:52:34.760
That was three times the number in 1959. In 1961, the net increase passed 100,000 for the first time. The BNP wanted to send all non-white immigrants back to their home countries. It also wanted to impeach the Conservative Cabinet and members of the 1945-50 Labour Cabinet for "complicity in the black invasion." The BNP had little money and few members, about 350. Yet its actions were highly sensational and grabbed headlines.

01:52:34.760 --> 01:52:40.307
It held demonstrations at London railway terminals to confront immigrants arriving from ports.

01:52:40.307 --> 01:53:14.269
It held two public meetings in Trafalgar Square. It also protested against the parade of a Jewish Lord Mayor of London and the Anti-Apartheid Movement. To expand into the provinces and attract younger members, the party started a paramilitary group called Spearhead. In 1961, the group held a summer camp on Fountaine's land. Twenty delegates from European nationalist groups attended. After a busy schedule of lectures, the participants celebrated their Nordic racial identity.

01:53:14.269 --> 01:53:28.861
They sang folk songs and drank traditional ale from tankards around the campfire. The immigration issue was a huge success for racial nationalism, but ideological splits were appearing in the BNP leadership.

01:53:28.861 --> 01:54:02.483
In February 1962, Bean put a resolution before the national council. It said that Jordan's wrong tactics focused too much on linking us to pre-war National Socialist Germany. This ignored the struggle for Britain, Europe, and the White World today and in the future. Bean and Fountaine clearly saw that Jordan's main drive was his admiration for Nazi Germany. He wanted to copy that example in modern Britain. This included all the trappings of swastikas, uniforms, and the Hitler cult.

01:54:02.483 --> 01:54:35.933
They believed this was a major political weakness. Britain had paid a heavy price in equipment and human lives in the Second World War. They wanted a modern British nationalist movement that dealt with 1960s issues. Jordan lost the vote 7 to 5. But he refused to step down. He reminded everyone that he had the exclusive right to use the Arnold Leese House. The BNP then split. Bean and Fountaine kept the party name, the magazine Combat, and over 80 percent of the members.

01:54:35.933 --> 01:54:50.525
Jordan kept the headquarters, John Tyndall, most of the Spearhead militia group, and the Birmingham and West Essex branches of the BNP. John Hutchyns Tyndall was born in 1934.

01:54:50.525 --> 01:55:19.283
His father was a Metropolitan police officer who moved from Ireland as a young man. The family came from County Waterford. They had a long history of service in the Royal Irish Constabulary. Tyndall served in the military in occupied Germany from 1952 to 1954. He then joined the LEL. He became a devoted reader of A. K. Chesterton's Candour magazine. This magazine focused on Jewish conspiracy theories.

01:55:19.283 --> 01:55:42.493
Tyndall believed that military strength helped maintain national awareness. He thought this was necessary to fight the damaging effects of liberalism. Tyndall had always preferred secret military training. This was true since he started leading his Spearhead group in the provinces on weekends. The Special Branch began watching Spearhead's activities in July 1961.

01:55:42.493 --> 01:56:14.664
Police found slogans like "Race War Now" and "Free Eichmann Now" on the wall of an old stable at Culverstone Green in Kent. Eichmann had recently been taken by Israeli agents from Argentina. He faced trial in Jerusalem for his role in the Final Solution. Tyndall and his lieutenant, Roland Kerr-Ritchie, were later seen drilling a group of eighteen men. The men wore Spearhead uniforms. These included gray shirts, armbands with a sun-wheel symbol, boots, and belts.

01:56:14.664 --> 01:56:20.979
Jordan renamed his small group the National Socialist Movement (NSM).

01:56:20.979 --> 01:56:56.733
He, John Tyndall, and Denis Pirie started to build a British neo-Nazi party. They gave it all the features of Hitlerism. Jordan launched the NSM at a party on 20 April 1962. That was Hitler's birthday. They served a cake decorated with a swastika. A transatlantic phone call to George Lincoln Rockwell, leader of the American Nazi Party, caused great excitement. They exchanged congratulations, "Heil Hitlers," and "Sieg Heils." Jordan gave a speech.

01:56:56.733 --> 01:57:34.280
He spoke of Britain's "loss and shame" for its role in the Second World War and the defeat of Hitler. He ended on a joyful note about the NSM's future. He said: "In Britain - in Britain of all places - the light which Hitler lit is burning, burning brighter, shining out across the waters, across the mountains, across the frontiers. National Socialism is coming back." In May, he began editing a new magazine, The National Socialist (1962-66).

01:57:34.280 --> 01:58:03.293
He also published the NSM manifesto. It stated: "The greatest treasure of the British people - the basis of their greatness in the past, and the only basis for it in the future - is their Aryan, predominantly Nordic blood; and that it is the first duty of the state to protect and improve this Island." Jordan's NSM stood out for its racial nationalism and praise of German National Socialism.

01:58:03.293 --> 01:58:34.696
These traits repeatedly made tabloid headlines in 1962. That year also saw public worry about immigration reach a peak. In the eighteen months before the new Immigration Act passed in July, about 212,000 colored immigrants entered Britain. On 1 July 1962, the NSM held a rally in Trafalgar Square. A crowd of four thousand attended. Jordan declared: "More and more people every day are opening their eyes and coming to see that Hitler was right.

01:58:34.696 --> 01:59:08.829
They are coming to see that our real enemies, the people we should have fought, were not Hitler and National Socialists of Germany but world Jewry and its associates in this country." John Tyndall delivered a similar anti-Semitic speech. He called the Jew "a poisonous maggot feeding off a body in an advanced state of decay" in our democratic society. This open display of Nazi views and hateful anti-Semitism overshadowed the main cause of colored immigration.

01:59:08.829 --> 01:59:15.144
The NSM followed the spirit of Arnold Leese and the interwar Imperial Fascist League.

01:59:15.144 --> 01:59:46.547
The rally ended in a riot. A large crowd of Jewish people, Communist Party members, and leftist CND (Campaign for Nuclear Disarmament) supporters stormed the platform. The NSM claimed that the rally started the racial conflict that summer. Oswald Mosley's Union Movement held rallies in July to protest colored immigration. These rallies took place in Trafalgar Square, Manchester, and the East End. All of them faced loud opposition and disorder.

01:59:46.547 --> 02:00:17.949
In early August, race riots lasted for three nights in Dudley, near Birmingham. Many arrests were made again. After the BNP split, Tyndall and Jordan kept up the paramilitary stormtrooper spirit in the NSM. In April and May 1962, detectives regularly watched Jordan as he led the Spearhead squad in military drills. These drills included mock attacks on an old tower at Leith Hill on the North Downs near Dorking in Surrey.

02:00:17.949 --> 02:00:48.669
This paramilitary training was a core part of NSM ideology. That ideology was based on the rise of the Nazis in Germany during the 1920s. Jordan and Tyndall were especially drawn to the romantic idea of armed struggle in a national crisis. The Spearhead drills also aimed to practice the skill, drill, and discipline of the British group. Jordan planned to host this group at the Nazi International camp in England in August 1962.

02:00:48.669 --> 02:00:53.619
Colin Jordan had two main reasons for holding this international Nazi conference.

02:00:53.619 --> 02:01:21.523
First, he wanted to raise the NSM's profile and grow its membership. When he split from the BNP, he had only about twenty activists left, including John Tyndall, Denis Pirie, and Roland Kerr-Ritchie. The Trafalgar Square rally kept the NSM in the public eye. But Jordan knew he needed more members. He especially wanted to compete with the BNP, which claimed one thousand active supporters. Jordan also had global ambitions.

02:01:21.523 --> 02:01:44.136
By bringing together foreign groups focused on racism and anti-Semitism under the NSM's banner, he aimed to lead an international Nazi movement. When Lincoln Rockwell attended the NSM summer camp at Guiting Wood, Gloucestershire, on 3-7 August 1962, he was likely the most notorious neo-Nazi in the world.

02:01:44.136 --> 02:02:14.429
His clownish tactics had earned him international news coverage. In these reports, he could regularly invoke the name of Adolf Hitler, quote Mein Kampf, and praise the Nazi crusade against Jews and all racial inferiors. The Home Office had banned Rockwell from entering Britain. Therefore, his secret attendance was another publicity win for the British leader. At the camp, Jordan wanted to impress his guest of honor with his own credentials for Nazi world leadership.

02:02:14.429 --> 02:02:49.928
On Sunday morning, Jordan showed his guests the military prowess and efficiency of the British Nazis. He did this by putting the Spearhead unit through its paces. John Tyndall led the unit. Uniformed NSM members deployed down the valley. They attacked sham strong-points, rushed imaginary enemy concentrations, and fought off make-believe counter-attacks. Meanwhile, Jordan, Rockwell, Savitri Devi, ex-SS lieutenant Fred Borth, and others watched the maneuvers through field glasses from high ground.

02:02:49.928 --> 02:03:16.808
The main event of the camp happened that afternoon and included all delegates. They created a new neo-Nazi international group called the World Union of National Socialists (WUNS). This followed the terms of the Cotswold Agreement. Under this agreement, Jordan, Rockwell, and the leaders of other foreign National Socialist parties formed a confederation. The WUNS had these major objectives: 1.

02:03:16.808 --> 02:03:46.845
To build a single, effective, international political group to fight and completely destroy the international Jewish-Communist and Zionist network of treason and subversion. 2. To protect and promote the Aryan race and its Western Civilization wherever its members are on the globe, regardless of their nationality. 3. To protect private property and free enterprise from Communist class warfare.

02:03:46.845 --> 02:03:56.659
Long-term goals included the "unity of all white people in a National Socialist world order with complete racial apartheid."

02:03:56.659 --> 02:04:21.320
Most other right-wing and nationalist groups would have found this acceptable. However, paragraph 7 of the twenty-five-paragraph codicil formally established the Nazi credentials of the WUNS. It stated: "No organization or individual failing to acknowledge the spiritual leadership of Adolf Hitler and the fact that we are National Socialists shall be admitted to membership."

02:04:21.320 --> 02:04:46.835
The long-term goal "to find and accomplish a just and final settlement of the Jewish problem" also identified the WUNS as a direct heir of Hitler's plans for a Final Solution. The twenty-seven delegates elected Jordan as world Führer and Rockwell as his deputy and heir. These delegates, along with their respective parties, became founding members of the WUNS.

02:04:46.835 --> 02:04:55.709
After the camp broke up in disorder due to an invasion by local villagers, Rockwell was arrested in London and deported back to the United States.

02:04:55.709 --> 02:05:24.296
Things got worse for the British Nazis. On Friday, 10 August, a dozen Special Branch officers raided and searched the NSM headquarters. The authorities' crackdown on the NSM effectively removed Colin Jordan from the center of WUNS activities early on after its birth. On 16 August, Jordan, Tyndall, Kerr-Ritchie, and Pirie were charged under the Public Order Act with organizing and equipping a paramilitary force.

02:05:24.296 --> 02:05:52.115
Jordan was sentenced to nine months' imprisonment, Tyndall to six, and their lieutenants to three each. Leadership of the WUNS now passed to George Lincoln Rockwell and the American Nazi Party. With its radical Nazi and anti-Semitic program, the WUNS soon succeeded in attracting many members of the Nouvel Ordre Européen (NOE), founded in 1951 in Zurich, into its own ranks.

02:05:52.115 --> 02:06:14.899
By the beginning of 1964, the WUNS announced that it maintained national sections in France, Germany, Great Britain, Belgium, Denmark, Switzerland, the United States, Argentina, Chile, and Australia. A new split repeated the earlier division between the BNP and the NSM.

02:06:14.899 --> 02:06:49.544
John Tyndall wanted to create a British form of national socialism. He emphasized patriotism, racial pride, and current conditions. He found Jordan's open worship of Hitler and careful copying of German Nazism increasingly out of date. He also saw it as a political weakness. Tyndall's bitter humiliation over losing his fiancée to Jordan also contributed to the break. In August 1964, Tyndall launched the Greater Britain Movement (GBM).

02:06:49.544 --> 02:07:16.424
It had its own magazine, Spearhead, and about 130 members. After their bitter split, both Jordan and Tyndall sought Rockwell's support. They wanted their party recognized as the British section of the WUNS. Rockwell instinctively sided with Jordan. Jordan had long promoted open Nazism. Rockwell was suspicious of Tyndall's plan to drop the swastika as a political symbol.

02:07:16.424 --> 02:07:52.264
The question of how openly one can embrace Nazi symbols has remained a lasting faultline in the development of the British far right. Feeling secure in Rockwell's support, Jordan built his reputation as the leading theorist of modern National Socialism in the Anglo-American world. In 1966, he wrote in the first issue of the WUNS journal National Socialist World. There, he gave an international readership a "philosophical appraisal" of universal Nazism.

02:07:52.264 --> 02:08:19.485
He argued that National Socialism had survived the defeat of the Third Reich and the later attacks on it. He said this was because it was "synonymous with higher man's will to survive, his instinct for health and strength, and his desire for beauty in life." Jordan traced its origins to Plato's Greece, Roman state service, and the feelings of blood kinship among the Nordic tribes.

02:08:19.485 --> 02:08:52.424
He saw National Socialism as a healthy, organic revolt. This revolt was "against the whole structure of thought of liberalism and democracy, with its cash nexus; its excessive individualism; its view of man as a folkless, interchangeable unit of world population; its spiritual justification in a debased Christianity embracing a sickly 'humanitarianism.'" He claimed that National Socialism was much more than a political scheme.

02:08:52.424 --> 02:09:06.845
It was a worldwide rebirth of the Aryan race and its folkfeeling, extending beyond the limits of nation states. After their split in 1964, Jordan stayed a hardline Nazi.

02:09:06.845 --> 02:09:36.029
Tyndall hid his past extremism behind British nationalism. In the 1964 general election, Jordan successfully campaigned on a racist platform for a Conservative candidate. This candidate ran against Patrick Gordon-Walker, Labour's intended foreign secretary, in Smethwick. Jordan copied Rockwell's tactic of using demonstrators in monkey suits to spread his racist message. He then ran his own campaign against Gordon-Walker.

02:09:36.029 --> 02:10:10.077
Gordon-Walker failed to win a seat again in the Leyton byelection of January 1965. Over the next two years, terrorism replaced electioneering. Behind the scenes, Nazi action commandos attacked Jewish properties. These groups came from Jordan's NSM, Fountaine's BNP, and Tyndall's GBM. They attacked thirty-four Jewish properties in the London area alone. They destroyed synagogues. They also firebombed a Jewish yeshiva (seminary) in Stoke Newington.

02:10:10.077 --> 02:10:40.883
A student died in that attack. NSM members were jailed for attacks on synagogues in Clapton, Ilford, Kilburn, and Bayswater. Jordan's wife, the French heiress Françoise Dior, was jailed for eighteen months in 1968. She conspired to burn a synagogue. Meanwhile, mainstream nationalists expected more support from the right after Labour won the 1966 general election and Labour and Tory policies on immigration became similar.

02:10:40.883 --> 02:10:48.819
Rockwell had formally recognized Jordan as the official British representative of the WUNS in early 1965.

02:10:48.819 --> 02:11:18.771
This frustrated Tyndall. He set aside his Nazi past and decided to build bridges within the radical right. His efforts paid off. He and members of the GBM were welcomed into A. K. Chesterton's new coalition. This coalition included the League of Empire Loyalists, the British National Party, and the Racial Preservation Society. They formed the National Front (NF) in February 1967.

02:11:18.771 --> 02:11:47.443
Chesterton intentionally excluded Jordan from these negotiations because of his embarrassing and open Nazism. Jordan therefore played no part in developing this new nationalist "fourth party" in British politics. This party achieved some significant electoral results in the 1970s in response to successive immigration scares. Jordan remained a man of the Nazi underground. How big was the NSM?

02:11:47.443 --> 02:12:04.765
In 1966, police records showed that the NSM had only 187 full members in its history. It also had several hundred supporters and subscribers to The National Socialist (1962-66).

02:12:04.765 --> 02:12:34.547
However, Searchlight claimed that 1,200 people were involved at some point. The group peaked at nearly 700 members in 1962. In January 1967, Jordan went to prison for the second time. The new Race Relations Act of 1965 led to his jail sentence. He served eighteen months for publishing an inflammatory pamphlet called The Coloured Invasion. This pamphlet aimed to promote racial strife.

02:12:34.547 --> 02:12:54.941
After his release, Jordan revived the defunct NSM as the British Movement in the summer of 1968. Unlike the NF, which sought parliamentary power, the British Movement (BM) focused on mobilizing skinheads, football hooligans, and young urban thugs.

02:12:54.941 --> 02:13:23.101
They targeted the left and colored immigrants in inner cities. This violent strategy echoed the "tough squads" of Leese's Imperial Fascist League. It also mirrored the Nazi stormtroopers of the 1920s. The BM used racial attacks to provoke West Indian and Asian minorities. They expected any counterattacks on whites to trigger a massive backlash. This would escalate into racial war.

02:13:23.101 --> 02:13:32.829
Jordan was succeeded as BM leader in 1974 by Michael McLaughlin, a former merchant seaman from Liverpool.

02:13:32.829 --> 02:14:00.989
McLaughlin was ambitious. He had clearly undermined Jordan's position while serving as chairman. In disgust, Jordan resigned from the BM entirely in 1975. He devoted himself to writing on his farm at Greenhow Hill near Harrogate, Yorkshire. Throughout the 1970s, the BM had close links with a political underground. This group fomented racial violence and sought contacts with European fascist terrorists.

02:14:00.989 --> 02:14:14.387
By 1980, the BM claimed to have twenty-five branches and a membership of four thousand. These figures probably counted skinheads, football hooligans, and other barely affiliated street fighters.

02:14:14.387 --> 02:14:47.325
However, McLaughlin's domain was difficult to govern. The presence of a turncoat and Searchlight mole, Ray Hill, at its highest levels thwarted many BM attacks. It also led to police investigations and much internal feuding. Once Ray Hill went public in 1982, the movement was severely demoralized. The unruliness of the BM street forces frustrated any proper internal organization. Despairing of an undisciplined rabble, McLaughlin resigned the leadership.

02:14:47.325 --> 02:14:56.883
He closed down the BM national office at Shotten in North Wales in late 1983. The remaining organizers rejected this disbandment.

02:14:56.883 --> 02:15:31.016
They began to save the movement. At its 1985 annual general meeting, they renamed it the British National Socialist Movement (BNSM). Jordan, the "godfather" of the Nazi underground, kept working to revive far-right terrorism. He was inspired by The Turner Diaries and the militant example of The Order in the United States. In June 1986, Jordan wrote a master plan for the future of British Nazism. He published it in the journal of the League of St. George.

02:15:31.016 --> 02:16:04.381
Jordan claimed that elites control television. This control ensures democracy survives through the ballot box and political parties. He rejected traditional party organization. He called for an "elite spearhead" or "task force" to replace it. This group would engage in "war." He mentioned the special units of Otto Skorzeny, the Third Reich's premier commando leader. Jordan argued that this armed guerrilla activity should match a racial populist party.

02:16:04.381 --> 02:16:33.224
That party should slowly build its respectability. Meanwhile, others should infiltrate mainstream parties and public bodies. Illegal activity often leads to capture and prison sentences. Jordan warned that "a strict separation of the personnel of the overt from those of the underground activities is absolutely essential." A few core BNSM activists clearly kept the movement alive, as Jordan described.

02:16:33.224 --> 02:17:03.603
First, they systematically re-recruited former members. They encouraged weapons training by placing BNSM members in gun clubs and Territorial Army units across the country. Several BNSM members with prior arms convictions joined Defence Begins At Home, a respectable right-wing pressure group also called the Hedgehogs. This group lobbied from 1983 to 1986 to boost Britain's community defense capability.

02:17:03.603 --> 02:17:33.384
The Blood and Honour network, which included about eight hundred skinheads who listened to white power music, offered another pool of recruits for BNSM recruiters. However, after the Hungerford massacre, where gun fanatic Michael Ryan killed his neighbors and police officers, even some BNSM members grew worried. After a tip-off, police arrested three leading BNSM gunmen while they fired pump-action shotguns in the Hertfordshire woods.

02:17:33.384 --> 02:17:56.765
These men were Jeff Carson, a scoutmaster from southwest London; David Philips from Essex; and John Sullivan from London. By this time, Northern Ireland's growing isolation in its nationalist struggle against both the Irish Republican Army (IRA) and a complacent U.K. government had begun to attract Britain's far right.

02:17:56.765 --> 02:18:24.157
They saw it as fertile ground for their own nationalist propaganda. The NF intensified its operations in the province. In November 1986, a massive joint NF-Orange Order march took place in Bridgwater, Somerset. This was the constituency of Northern Ireland secretary Tom King. The march protested the Anglo-Irish Agreement. The BNSM forged its own military links with Ulster Loyalist groups.

02:18:24.157 --> 02:18:36.531
These included the Ulster Defence Association (UDA) and its terrorist units, the Ulster Freedom Fighters (UFF) and the Ulster Volunteer Force (UVF).

02:18:36.531 --> 02:19:08.019
These groups operated in both Northern Ireland and mainland Britain. Underground BNSM members were frequently involved in gun-running and armed attacks against Republican targets there. The Blood and Honour network also provided further BNSM recruits for the mainland cells of the Ulster units. John Nicholson, a lay preacher in the Protestant Church and a London UDA officer, arranged for the training of dozens of young men in southern England.

02:19:08.019 --> 02:19:13.309
Finally, the BNSM built close ties with neo-Nazi groups on the continent.

02:19:13.309 --> 02:19:48.637
Et Wolsink, born in 1924, was a former Dutch SS member. He became the BNSM international liaison officer. He also joined several neo-Nazi groups. These included a senior role in the Dutch People's Union (DVU), the Dutch "Wiking Jugend," the Northern League, and the Dutch section of the German neo-Nazi ANS-NA, led by Michael Kühnen. Wolsink had a notorious Nazi past. In 1946, he was sentenced to eight years in prison for his role in the SS Brandenburg division.

02:19:48.637 --> 02:20:16.712
He was a close friend of the widow of Dutch Nazi leader Rost van Tonningen. In April 1989, Wolsink gathered over one hundred BNSM members and overseas supporters at a secret location in Derbyshire. They marked the hundredth anniversary of Hitler's birthday. By 1990, the two to three hundred active BNSM members were concentrated in London, the Midlands, and especially Yorkshire.

02:20:16.712 --> 02:20:49.992
Two leaders, Stephen Frost and Glyn Fordham, operated from P.O. boxes in Slaithwaite near Huddersfield and Heckmondwike. Colin Jordan lived nearby on his Yorkshire farm. He always kept up with developments among the militant Nazis. Jordan kept writing articles for American Nazi publications. He wrote about the current relevance of National Socialism and the unique leadership of Adolf Hitler. In National Socialism: World Creed for the 1980s

02:20:49.992 --> 02:21:09.448
(1981), a booklet reprinted from an article first published in the WUNS periodical, Jordan dismissed nationalists, populists, Nazi fetishists ("Hollywood Nazis"), and skinheads as betrayers of National Socialism.

02:21:09.448 --> 02:21:41.875
This was a sideswipe at those street fighters initially welcomed into the British Movement. Jordan exalted Nazism as a religion of life and nature. He said it was quite incompatible with Christianity. He concluded that National Socialists were neither nationalists nor conservatives. They were racial revolutionaries. They summoned the white peoples of the world to unite for survival and supremacy. As a current tactic, he argued for disruptive sabotage of the system.

02:21:41.875 --> 02:21:56.125
He also argued for the development of elite Nazi cadres through private Nazi schools, labor projects, and small rural communities. This idea continued into a back-to-the-land movement.

02:21:56.125 --> 02:22:33.075
It involved "Political Soldier" and "Third Way" activists. These groups emerged from the National Front's breakup in the mid-1980s. Nick Griffin, a former NF leader, trained cadres at his family farm in Suffolk. The political soldiers sought new alliances. They made overtures to Qaddafi's Libya, Iran, and Iraq. The group also praised the Welsh nationalist bombers and arsonists, the Sons of Glyndwr. From his farm on the Welsh Marches, Griffin ran a "Smash the Cities" campaign.

02:22:33.075 --> 02:23:08.061
This implied a Nazi version of Pol Potism. David Myatt, one of Jordan's devoted followers in the old BM, tried to set up a Nazi country commune in Shropshire. In the 1990s, the Order of Jarls Bælder, Myatt's Reichs-folk, and the National Socialist Alliance mounted similar rural ventures. They aimed to foster the elite Nazi spirit among the few. These few were expected to lead the masses when the established social and economic order ultimately collapses (see chapter 11).

02:23:08.061 --> 02:23:24.872
In the early 1980s, Jordan revived Leese's periodical Gothic Ripples. He used it as his own occasional outlet for articles on the Third Reich, Hess's "murder" in Spandau prison, and anti-Semitic and racist views on current events.

02:23:24.872 --> 02:23:50.131
Praise for Hitler was a regular feature in these writings. This praise peaked in 1989, the centenary of his birth. "Hitler was Right!" first appeared in Gothic Ripples. It was later reprinted in George Dietz's special 20 April 1989 anniversary issue of Liberty Bell. The article defended Hitler's accuracy on many issues.

02:23:50.131 --> 02:24:06.685
These included his criticism of democracy, his protection of the folk community, his claimed preemptive attack on the Soviet Union, the missed chance for an Anglo-German alliance, and his prediction of the dark age that would follow his defeat.

02:24:06.685 --> 02:24:34.675
In a commemorative article for Matt Koehl's New Order NS Bulletin, Jordan followed Savitri Devi's explanation. He presented Hitler as a "Man against Time." He described him as a superhuman personality who used his own will to fight Aryan decline within the cycle of the ages. The magazine of the League of St. George, a leading far-right group in Britain, also published another hymn to Hitler.

02:24:34.675 --> 02:25:07.187
Arno Breker, a Nazi sculptor, created the dark, muscular bronze statues that decorate Jordan's booklets and articles on National Socialism. These works target a literate audience. Compared to the pious and enthusiastic writings of the New Order, this native British testimony to Hitler and universal Nazism feels earnest and down to earth. In A Train of Thought (1989), Jordan returned to the theme of clandestine task forces.

02:25:07.187 --> 02:25:39.869
He aimed to speed the breakdown of the social order. This hope now rested with the underground BNSM. In 1993, he lightened his touch with a satire called Merrie England - 2,000. The book paints a droll Orwellian view of late twentieth-century Britain. It shows a country dominated by the race-relations police. It includes reeducation for bigoted elderly people. It offers tax relief for mixed marriages. It demands ritual obeisance from the guilty white population.

02:25:39.869 --> 02:26:03.677
It replaces Nelson's Column with a statue of Nelson Mandela in "Harmony Square." In recognition of his godfather status to the international Nazi movement over three decades, the European section of the WUNS in Denmark published a volume of Jordan's selected writings in 1993. Combat 18 is a guerrilla group active since the early 1990s.

02:26:03.677 --> 02:26:37.981
It revived Colin Jordan's plan for a militant Nazi underground. The group descends directly from the BNSM in both personnel and methods. Combat 18, or C18, mobilizes thugs, boot boys, and skinheads. They carry out physical attacks, bombings, and arson against their perceived racial enemies. The name comes from the first and eighth letters of the alphabet. These letters signify Adolf Hitler. C18 specializes in intimidation, harassment, and brutality.

02:26:37.981 --> 02:27:13.224
Attacks are usually followed by gloating phone calls. They also use crude stickers bearing the group's black skull symbol. The stickers carry the caption "Combat 18 in the area." Illustrated fliers show a sinister trooper wearing a gas mask. He carries powerful new weapons. The fliers are captioned "C18 ready for ethnic cleansing" in cut-out letters. C18 is an armed criminal conspiracy. It gathers intelligence and mobilizes its cells. They carry out acts of violence against chosen targets.

02:27:13.224 --> 02:27:47.613
These targets have included Labour politicians, MPs, green activists, and members of Jewish organizations. The group distributes hit lists containing its enemies' private addresses and telephone numbers. It aims to strike fear into all opponents. It shows that it is always ready to mount surprise attacks. C18 started to form in late 1991. It grew out of the BNSM, Blood and Honour skinhead groups, and notorious racist football gangs.

02:27:47.613 --> 02:27:55.976
These gangs included West Ham, Charlton, Leeds, Millwall, and the Chelsea Headhunters.

02:27:55.976 --> 02:28:30.536
Harold A. Covington, an American Nazi, lived in London that winter. He appears to have played a key role in encouraging a new militant Nazi alliance. This alliance involved groups in Sweden, Germany, and C18 in Britain. They used computer communications and U.S.-style Nazi terrorism. Another factor helped the group. BNP meetings and other events needed tougher security. This included lectures by the revisionist historian David Irving in November 1991.

02:28:30.536 --> 02:28:40.861
In February 1992, C18 carried out a brutal and bloody attack on Anti-Nazi League pamphleteers at Tower Hamlets.

02:28:40.861 --> 02:29:12.264
Old BNSM members and known football hooligans began to guard the BNP. They protected it as it canvassed London streets and ran election rallies. This happened in the run-up to the April 1992 general election. Because of its subversive and illegal activities, C18 used an offshore mailing address in Raleigh, North Carolina. This was Covington's Dixie Press. Covington then passed applications and inquiries back to Steve Sargent in Barnet.

02:29:12.264 --> 02:29:35.475
Sargent's Resurgam Books also distributed the Searchlight article on Covington's earlier role in Britain. Paul David Sargent (b. 1960) was the unchallenged street leader of C18. People better knew him as Charlie "Ginger Pig" Sargent because of his hair color and plump figure.

02:29:35.475 --> 02:30:09.949
Charlie Sargent was a typical working-class Nazi thug. He was active in the BM during the 1970s and early 1980s. He had a long record of violence. In 1978, courts convicted him of offensive weapons and threatening behavior charges linked to public disorders. He proclaimed a "race war." He incited Muslims and blacks to retaliate with violence. If others did not follow him, he would know that "our race is too weak to survive and deserves to die."

02:30:09.949 --> 02:30:44.424
His elder brother, William, was active in the National Front. William organized illegal dogfights. His younger brother, Stephen, ran Resurgam Books. Stephen published Thor-Would, a pagan C18 magazine, from his home in Barnet. Eddy Whicker was another top figure in C18. He was a South London garbage collector. In the 1970s, he was one of the National Front's toughest street fighters. Whicker was later involved with the UDA, as was Charlie Sargent.

02:30:44.424 --> 02:31:18.984
Whicker has been a prominent steward in C18-minding activities alongside the BNP. John Merritt and Paul Ballard were also senior C18 managers. Both were long-term members of the Croydon BNP branch, a former NF stronghold. Steve Martin from Stamford Hill was another C18 man. He also had BNP and strong Ulster loyalist links. Once charged with UVF gun running, he later became a full UDA member. The C18 Redwatch bulletins contained lists of enemies.

02:31:18.984 --> 02:31:49.021
This was a clear call to violence, injury, and murder. The first issue (March 1992) was labeled "a bimonthly report on the red front. Compiled by COMBAT 18." It carried the slogan "let them hate so long as they fear." Readers were told to make their own lists. The American Nazi model was clear in references to the Aryan Militant group. It also included unexpected attacks with knives and guns.

02:31:49.021 --> 02:31:57.640
One instruction said "to hide in the faceless hordes of ZOGs putrid, mud infested cities …

02:31:57.640 --> 02:32:34.931
UNDERMINE-DEMORALIZE-DESTROY." Many people listed in the second issue (May 1992) were not communists. They were Labour Party members, officers of refugee organizations, and anti-apartheid activists. A press release described C18's arson attack on the Morning Star office. The final page placed the words "race war" and "armed resistance" over a portrait of Hitler and a sketch of a masked figure with an assault rifle. The C18 skull logo was also on that page.

02:32:34.931 --> 02:33:01.469
The fire at the communist newspaper served as a model for new attacks. Two arsons in Birmingham were listed in later Redwatch issues. These were the Democratic Left office (August 1992) and the Sandwell Unemployment and Community Resource Centre (November 1992). In these rough, poorly written bulletins, C18 showed off its Nazi ideas.

02:33:01.469 --> 02:33:31.592
The third issue of Redwatch carried the symbol of the South African Afrikaner Weerstandsbeweging (AWB) movement. It also had the caption "Zyklon-B: over six million satisfied customers. Manufactured by Combat 18" next to a picture of an Auschwitz poison gas canister. The hit list named several Communist Party organizers, ANC supporters, and gave information on the left-wing group Militant.

02:33:31.592 --> 02:34:01.800
The fourth issue listed Ken Livingstone, the Labour council leader; Marc Wadsworth of the Anti-Racist Alliance; and Sir Ivan Lawrence QC, the Conservative MP and member of the Jewish Board of Deputies who had recently become chairman of the Home Affairs select committee on race relations. The third issue of another C18 magazine called Combat 18 gave detailed instructions on how to make powerful bombs, explosives, and fuses.

02:34:01.800 --> 02:34:35.677
Under the slogan "Kill em all!," C18 target lists now included Paddy Ashdown, the Liberal Democratic Party leader; Glenda Jackson, the well-known actress and prominent Labour supporter; Alf Lomas, a member of the European Parliament; and Paul Condon, commissioner of the Metropolitan Police and a senior detective of the International and Organised Crime Branch, the unit specially assigned to deal with C18 crimes. C18 had two to three hundred members across Britain.

02:34:35.677 --> 02:35:06.909
They operated in military cells. They caused hundreds of criminal incidents, including affray, arson, and violent assault. Asian businesses in London were burned down. Trades unionists' homes in Durham and Leeds were destroyed. A firebomb hit a meeting in Milton Keynes. Leon Greenman, an eighty-year-old Holocaust survivor, was speaking there. He was later harassed. A demonstration in Eltham happened in November 1992.

02:35:06.909 --> 02:35:26.109
This was followed by affray in Nottingham on 23 January 1993. Left-wing and anarchist bookshops in Kilburn, Whitechapel, Nottingham, and Durham were attacked. On 15 January 1994, C18 organized a large international skinhead event.

02:35:26.109 --> 02:36:00.584
Neo-Nazi groups from Holland, Denmark, and Germany took part. The event turned into running battles across London. Left-wing protesters and the police were involved. In August 1994 in Leeds, crossbow and firebomb attacks hit ANL members. Derek Fatchett, the Labour MP for Leeds West, was granted police protection twice. Over three years, dozens of incidents occurred in London alone. These involved arson and vicious assaults against colored people.

02:36:00.584 --> 02:36:32.669
Many of these were reported in successive issues of the new C18 magazines, Putsch, Lebensraum and The Order. The reports boasted of injury and damage. Putsch and Lebensraum show the frustration and rage of white working-class young people. They have been pushed out of their traditional neighborhoods by growing racial minorities. Thirty years and a whole generation after Jordan's first race riots, Britain now has large, established Asian and black communities.

02:36:32.669 --> 02:37:07.485
These communities are in London and the large cities of the North and Midlands. Mosques and Hindu temples have replaced old pubs and labor clubs. Ethnic festivals overwhelm white residents who feel under threat. Asian-language newspapers, cinemas, and shops show that large unassimilated groups exist. White young people form a tiny minority in many schools. The student rolls in these schools are almost exclusively made up of ethnic minority children.

02:37:07.485 --> 02:37:15.848
Housing allocations in London boroughs like Tower Hamlets give too much space to the ethnic population.

02:37:15.848 --> 02:37:49.469
This happens out of all proportion to their white residents. This has led to a "rights for whites" movement. The British National Party leads this movement. Labour-held councils now select Muslim candidates for office in areas with high Asian populations. Many local authorities favor blacks in employment, special projects, and facilities. They even favor blacks for mayoral office. Working-class whites face the increasing cultural and political self-assertion of minorities directly.

02:37:49.469 --> 02:37:56.381
John Cato's editorial line in Putsch plays on the fears of poor, white, working-class youth.

02:37:56.381 --> 02:38:24.797
These young people face growing threats of being pushed aside. He attacks liberal elites for conspiring to strip them of their inheritance. He blames political correctness and public spending on multicultural festivals, black AIDS research, homosexual clubs, and police training in racial sensitivity and minority languages. He compares the fate of black slaves to the suffering of the Victorian working class.

02:38:24.797 --> 02:38:32.307
He asks why the white working class should share the guilt of the liberal middle classes over racism.

02:38:32.307 --> 02:39:04.733
White youth clubs are closing down. Large parts of urban areas are being handed over to ethnic groups. The media and mass entertainment blast a constant stream of positive multiracial images at the British public. At the same time, the national press constantly hides reports of black-on-white crime and racial conflict in inner cities. Rare white racist attacks on blacks get heavy coverage filled with guilt and moralizing.

02:39:04.733 --> 02:39:35.795
Many white victims of black crime are simply blamed on poor "race relations." Cato demands the mass return of colored immigrants. He argues that the multiracial experiment is a total disaster. He claims it is kept alive only by a controlled media and pious liberal elites. The C18 hit lists, bomb-making instructions, and rising racial violence show the influence of American Nazi ideas and methods. In The Order,

02:39:35.795 --> 02:40:08.904
a magazine named after the U.S. terrorist group, editor John Cato praised its dead leader, Robert Jay Mathews. He quoted Mathews's "declaration of war" against a "Jewish controlled mongrelized society, which is depriving White Aryans of their existence and homeland." That same issue explained Louis Beam's strategy of "leaderless resistance" for the war on ZOG. In the pages of Putsch, Cato rejoiced in Pierce's call for individual acts of violence against blacks and Jews.

02:40:08.904 --> 02:40:33.395
After fleeing from Kent to Spalding in Lincolnshire, Cato started a new magazine, The Oak, which reprinted many of Pierce's articles. Paul Jeffries set up Life Rune Books in Leeds as the U.K. distributor for William Pierce's National Alliance. In June 1994, Cato and Jeffries formed the National Socialist Alliance (NSA).

02:40:33.395 --> 02:41:05.651
This was a federation of C18, several rebel BNSM sections with their magazines Sigrun and Europe Awake,, and the Blood and Honour groups. It served as a British version of Pierce's American organization. By mid-1995, several smaller groups had joined the NSA. These included David Myatt's National-Socialist Movement, Adrian Blundell's White Aryan Resistance, and the Yorkshire-based Patriotic Women's League.

02:41:05.651 --> 02:41:25.619
The NSA also adopted other American ideas, including terrorism, "leaderless resistance," and contact with the National Alliance. The concept of an "Aryan white homeland," known from The Turner Diaries and Christian Identity beliefs, started to spread among young British Nazis.

02:41:25.619 --> 02:41:58.216
They rejected an island off the Scottish coast. Instead, they chose an area that was sparsely populated, almost entirely white, and close enough to large cities to wage war against a multiracial society. They decided to build this racial homeland in Essex, between Chelmsford and the coast, near the Bradwell nuclear power station. Colin Jordan's former NSM aide, Wulstram Tedder, supported the idea. He was already running a small Nazi commune on the Welsh borders.

02:41:58.216 --> 02:42:30.899
David Myatt, another violent former BM activist and Nazi satanist, also backed the project. He promoted it as the "East Saxon Kindred." This was to be "an all-White neighbourhood and community, and thus an Aryan republic …where Aryans can live among their own kind …the territory will thus be ruled and controlled by Aryans who are National-Socialists." The NSA's formation happened as the British far-right grew more radical.

02:42:30.899 --> 02:42:38.835
The BNP won a council seat in Tower Hamlets in September 1993, then lost it in May 1994.

02:42:38.835 --> 02:43:10.152
This led to frustration with electoral strategy, especially among younger members. Racist groups felt besieged. They faced the widespread acceptance of a multiracial society and stricter enforcement of race-relations laws. These laws led to the imprisonment of leaders and the censorship of their press. The turn toward sectarian militancy and enclave doctrine mirrored the development of American Nazism in the late 1970s and early 1980s.

02:43:10.152 --> 02:43:18.429
British Nazis now declared an all-out battle for the survival of the white race against the hated ZOG.

02:43:18.429 --> 02:43:48.467
They spoke with religious fervor and apocalyptic prophecy. The masthead of Putsch magazine carried the motto "we must secure the existence of our people and a future for white children." These are the "14 Words" of David Lane. Lane was a member of The Order. He is serving a life sentence for his part in the murder of a Jewish radio commentator in Denver. In early 1995, more regional BNP members defected to the NSA.

02:43:48.467 --> 02:44:09.629
This included the Halifax, Oldham, Scotland, and Northern Ireland branches. Since it started, C18 has been closely linked to neo-Nazi groups abroad. In 1992, Harold Covington established contacts with the terrorist group White Aryan Resistance (VAM) in Sweden.

02:44:09.629 --> 02:44:40.264
This underground group copies The Order. It robs banks and stockpiles weapons. These are preliminary steps for a "racial holocaust" to "eliminate ZOG." Its declared enemies are political parties, the police, the media, the Jewish community, and anti-racists. In December 1993, neo-Nazi letter-bomb campaigns began in Austria. They targeted socialists and liberals who were soft on immigration.

02:44:40.264 --> 02:44:51.187
Cryptic messages from the Bavarian Liberation Army (Bajuvarische Befreiungsarmee, BBA) regularly cite heroes from Austria's military past.

02:44:51.187 --> 02:45:25.917
These heroes fought invading Avars, Slavs, and Turks. Like VAM, the German anti-anti-fascist organization also publishes a hit-list bulletin, Der Einblick, across the border in Denmark. Both organizations foster contacts with C18 and the Danish National Socialist Movement (Dansk Nasjonal Sosjalistik Bewegung, DNSB). They do this at the annual international Nazi festival in Diksmuide and the Rudolf Hess commemorations in Fulda.

02:45:25.917 --> 02:45:51.347
Leading members of the DNSB, VAM, NSA, and Norwegian and Austrian groups met in Copenhagen in March 1995. They coordinated their anti-anti-fascist activities. Strong evidence of these international links appeared in January 1997. Seven young Danish neo-Nazis faced charges for planning an international letter-bombing campaign.

02:45:51.347 --> 02:46:26.077
They targeted people in London, with targets supplied by C18. The group planned to post the packages in Sweden. They borrowed the letter-bomb technique directly from Austrian nationalists. However, the British targets showed the influence of American "race war" ideas. The intended recipients included prominent British athletes in mixed-race marriages. Kriss Akabusi and Derek Redmond were among them. Targeting such "race-traitors" and their spouses was a key theme in William Pierce's novel Hunter.

02:46:26.077 --> 02:46:55.091
In that book, the Nazi hero stalked race-mixing couples with the intent to kill. He did this to spread terror and demoralization throughout multiracial society. C18 mobilized their Danish, Swedish, and German allies for this violent campaign. They aimed it at politicians and public figures. This shows the international scope of the hit-list strategy. That strategy intends to intimidate all supporters of multiracialism.

02:46:55.091 --> 02:47:02.344
Only weeks after the bombing campaign was exposed, Charlie Sargent was charged with murdering a fellow activist.

02:47:02.344 --> 02:47:33.917
He is now serving a long prison sentence. C18 began to fall apart. At the same time, Troy Southgate's National Revolutionary Faction was gaining prominence in the militant underground. Southgate started his political career in 1983 with the "Political Soldiers" faction of the National Front. In 1989, he followed Griffin and others into the Italian-inspired International Third Position. This association lasted until September 1992.

02:47:33.917 --> 02:48:11.805
Then Southgate formed the English Nationalist Movement (ENM). Between 1992 and 1998, the ENM returned to the revolutionary principles of the NF. It emphasized the writings of Otto Strasser and Walther Darré. It also emphasized the socialist ideas of William Morris, Robert Owen, and William Cobbett. In 1998, the party was renamed the National Revolutionary Faction (NRF). The NRF is committed to "national revolution." It advocates a strong Europe.

02:48:11.805 --> 02:48:42.269
It has joined the European Liberation Front. This is a pan-European alliance of national revolutionaries. It is based on the ideas of Otto Strasser, Francis Parker Yockey, and Jean Thiriart. Like other groups in the Euro-American radical right, the NRF is committed to fighting the ZOG and the "New World Order." It rejects the democratic process. It aims to establish autonomous all-white zones.

02:48:42.269 --> 02:49:18.195
In August 2000, its strategy of infiltration led to joint actions with violent anti-hunt saboteurs of the Animal Liberation Front. David Myatt's National-Socialist Movement (NSM) took in many C18 activists when Charlie Sargent's younger brother, Steve, and a few dozen supporters joined the NSM in March 1997. David Myatt, a long-time follower of right-wing extremism and satanism, started developing a "religion of National-Socialism" in the early 1990s.

02:49:18.195 --> 02:49:47.208
He advertised his writings in The Oak, edited by John Cato. Myatt pushed for direct action and sabotage of basic services like water, sewage, and electricity. He saw C18 as the street army needed to build an Aryan revolutionary movement. Myatt's cult-like view of Nazism held a Manichaean view of the racial struggle between Aryans and the growing numbers of colored groups in British cities.

02:49:47.208 --> 02:50:03.592
He wrote: "Since these foreigners are an invasion force, since there is now a war, and since we do live under a tyrannical Zionist Occupation Government, we have no choice but to actively fight for our freedom, our race and our lands.

02:50:03.592 --> 02:50:30.984
We must fight the non-Aryan invaders who have settled in our lands." Because Myatt's strengths lay in political education and doctrine, Tony Williams (b. 1956) took over leadership of the expanded NSM in 1997. Williams was a wealthy young supporter of Nazi causes since the early 1980s. The NSM was refounded in June 1997.

02:50:30.984 --> 02:51:06.824
It stayed true to Myatt's visionary Hitlerism. It was committed to creating an exclusive Aryan community in Britain. The NSM rejected the "conventionalities of electioneering." It adopted the Nazi leadership principle to foster "national and racial solidarity, duty and honour." Tony Williams started publishing Column 88. This was a quarterly magazine in color. His editorials, "Broadcasts from the Bunker," offered a flippant commentary on liberal Britain as seen from the Third Reich.

02:51:06.824 --> 02:51:41.128
The magazine featured historical articles on Nazi social welfare in prewar Germany. It also covered the life of William Joyce. These alternated with Myatt's views on suppressing dissent in democracies. They also included a eulogy by U.S. convict Steve Stein for young German Panzer crews. The magazine ran features on NSM policy regarding racial identity and community values. It also included an interview with Colin Jordan. It published excerpts from the writings of Savitri Devi.

02:51:41.128 --> 02:52:12.957
It told heroic stories of German military exploits in World War II. Williams focused on history and philosophy. Steve Sargent continued publishing White Dragon. This was a bimonthly magazine. It targeted skinheads and football fans with a white ethnic message. The NSM gained national attention when it emerged that the young man arrested for the three nail bombings in London in May 1999 had joined the group in late 1998.

02:52:12.957 --> 02:52:40.520
David Copeland (b. 1976) lived in isolated, multiracial single-room housing in East London. He embraced racist politics, joined the British National Party in spring 1997, and read Christian Identity literature online. By 1996, Copeland had started planning a bombing campaign against ethnic groups to provoke a backlash and racial war in Britain.

02:52:40.520 --> 02:52:56.307
Seeking more radical contacts, he joined the NSM and became an area leader in February 1999. On 19 April, his first nail-bomb attack in Brixton, a largely black London borough, wounded thirty-nine people.

02:52:56.307 --> 02:53:30.611
On 24 April, he attacked Brick Lane, an area with an Asian population, leaving six people wounded. On 30 April, he bombed a public house in Soho frequented by homosexuals. This attack killed three people and horrifically injured sixty-five others. Allegedly inspired by The Turner Diaries, Copeland acted as a lone wolf and had little involvement with the NSM. Panicked by the discovery of the bomber's identity, Tony Williams disbanded the NSM in May 1999.

02:53:30.611 --> 02:53:45.971
However, Copeland's violent campaign was a textbook application of "leaderless resistance" and operation in "phantom cells." The Nazi underground has stayed active in Britain from the early 1960s to today.

02:53:45.971 --> 02:54:20.189
It has kept spreading racist anti-Semitism. It has tried to start violent fights between white people and people of color in British cities. The loud protests, angry speech, and crimes of the original NSM, BM, and C18 groups have had a huge effect. These groups carried out racial attacks, arson, and sabotage. Their influence on anti-immigrant feelings and even government policy is far larger than their actual membership numbers suggest.

02:54:20.189 --> 02:54:51.677
Copeland saw his nail-bomb campaign as a provocation for racial war. This militant tradition owes much to Colin Jordan, the godfather of British neo-Nazism. His time in prison radicalized him. Jordan has always pushed for the growth of revolutionary Nazi activist cells. He wants to overthrow liberal democracy during times of crisis. Like his American counterparts, Jordan combined a deep love of Hitler and the Third Reich with a modern racist doctrine.

02:54:51.677 --> 02:55:12.499
This doctrine opposes colored populations within white nations. Like American neo-Nazism, this British Hitlerism aims at global white supremacy. It does this through a campaign of millenarian militancy. This militancy targets the perceived disorders of liberalism and multiracialism.

02:55:12.499 --> 02:55:12.599

